Shaumari&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La Réserve Faunique de Shaumari est une réserve naturelle jordanienne située près de la ville d’Azraq, à environ 100 km à l’est de Amman. Il s&#039;agit d&#039;une ré...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;fr/reserve-faunique-de-shaumari/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Lire Plus&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Natural Reserves/wetland.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Réserve de Zones Humides Azraq&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt;  Réserve de Zones Humides Azraq&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La Réserve de Zones Humides Azraq est une réserve naturelle située près de la ville d&#039;Azraq, dans le désert oriental de la Jordanie. Une oasis pour le...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;fr/reserve-de-zones-humides-azraq/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Lire Plus&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Natural Reserves/Yarmouk.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Réserve Forestière de Yarmouk&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt;  Réserve Forestière de Yarmouk&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La &lt;span&gt;Royal Society for the Conservation of Nature&lt;/span&gt; est en train de mettre en œuvre la gestion intégrée des écosystèmes dans le projet de la vallée du Jourda...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;fr/reserve-forestiere-de-yarmouk/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Lire Plus&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Natural Reserves/River-canyon-of-Wadi-Mujib.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Wadi Mujib&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt;  Wadi Mujib&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;En 2011, l&#039;UNESCO a déclaré la réserve de biosphère du Mujib. Il s&#039;étend jusqu&#039;aux montagnes de Kerak et de Madaba au nord et au sud, atteignant 900...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;fr/wadi-mujib/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Lire Plus&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/more places/Irbid.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Irbid&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt;  Irbid&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Irbid est la deuxième plus grande ville de Jordanie. Une courte promenade dans le célèbre musée Dar As-Saraya révèle les origines anciennes d&#039;Irbid. Le...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;fr/irbid/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Lire Plus&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/more places/Jerash2.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Jerash&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt;  Jerash&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Jerash, située à 48 km au nord d&#039;Amman et nichée dans une vallée paisible entre les montagnes de Gilead, est la grandeur de la Rome impériale et const...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;fr/jerash/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Lire Plus&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/more places/800px-AS-SALT_2.png&quot; alt=&quot;Al-Salt&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt;  Al-Salt&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Al-Salt est une ville prospère située dans le nord-ouest de la capitale, Amman. Construit sur trois montagnes principales (Cadital, Gadaa et Salalem), entouré par la...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;fr/al-salt/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Lire Plus&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/more places/1024px-Umayyad_Palace020.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Ummayyad Palace&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt;  Ummayyad Palace&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Le Umayyad Palace est un grand complexe palatial de la période des Omeyyades, situé sur la colline de la citadelle d&#039;Amman, en Jordanie. Construit au cour...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;fr/ummayyad-palace/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Lire Plus&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/more places/Karak.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Karak&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt;  Karak&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Connu au cours de l&#039;histoire sous les noms de Qir Heres, Qir Moab et Hareseth, Karak a été une possession précieuse de plusieurs civilisations. Il est situé sur...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;fr/karak/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Lire Plus&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 387, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'ou-aller-en-jordanie'),
(395, 'Desert Castles', 'Desert Castles', 'Learn more about the traces of historical civilizations and more recent constructions left in the desert of the East of Jordan.', 'desert castles, eastern desert Jordan, East of Jordan', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Stretching East of Amman, the parched desert plain rolls on to Iraq and Saudi Arabia. This is a place where endless sand and barren basalt landscapes give proof to man’s ability to thrive under harsh conditions.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The discovery of flint hand-axes in this desert indicates that Paleolithic settlers inhabited the region around half a million years ago. But the most remarkable remains of human habitation are the palaces built by the Damascus-based Umayyad caliphs during the early days of Islam (VII-VIII centuries CE).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;During the height of the Umayyad dynasty, architecture flourished with the cultural exchange that accompanied growing trade routes. By 750 CE, when the Umayyad dynasty was overthrown by the Abbasids of Baghdad, a richly characteristic Muslim architecture was evolving, owing considerably to the cosmopolitan influence of builders and craftsmen drawn from Egypt, Mesopotamia and elsewhere throughout the region.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Today it is possible to see many relics of the early and medieval Islamic periods in Jordan. Dotted throughout the steppe-like terrain of eastern Jordan and the central hills are numerous historic ruins, including castles, forts, towers, baths, caravan inns and fortified palaces. Known collectively as the desert castles, they were originally part of a chain stretching from north of Damascus down to Khirbet al-Mafjar, near Ariha (or Jericho).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;en/qasr-al-kharanah/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Qasr Al-Kharanah&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;en/qasr-amra/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Qasr Amra&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Desert Castles/qasr-amra.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3202.960326365759!2d36.46056488753891!3d31.7285686252473!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b249e0321d58d:0xae2394f52625c2b!2sQasr al-Kharaneh!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569247005481!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 395, 'en', '', 'one col', 'desert-castles'),
(396, 'Les Chateaux Du Desert', 'Les Chateaux Du Desert', 'S&#039;étendant à l&#039;est d&#039;Amman, la plaine aride du désert se poursuit jusqu&#039;en Irak et en Arabie Saoudite.', 'S&#039;étendant à l&#039;est d&#039;Amman, la plaine aride du désert se poursuit jusqu&#039;en Irak et en Arabie Saoudite.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;S&#039;étendant à l&#039;est d&#039;Amman, la plaine aride du désert se poursuit jusqu&#039;en Irak et en Arabie Saoudite. C’est un endroit où des paysages infinis de sable et de basalte stérile témoignent de la capacité de l’homme à s’épanouir dans des conditions difficiles.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La découverte de haches en silex dans ce désert indique que les colons du Paléolithique ont habité la région il y a environ un demi-million d&#039;années. Mais les vestiges humains les plus remarquables sont les palais construits par les califes omeyyades basés à Damas pendant les premiers jours de l&#039;islam (VII-VIII siècles de notre ère).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Au plus fort de la dynastie des Omeyyades, l&#039;architecture s&#039;épanouit grâce aux échanges culturels qui accompagnèrent les routes commerciales en pleine croissance. En 750 de notre ère, lorsque les Abbassides de Bagdad ont renversé la dynastie des Omeyyades, une architecture musulmane aux caractéristiques riches évoluait, en raison notamment de l&#039;influence cosmopolite des constructeurs et artisans d&#039;Egypte, de Mésopotamie et d&#039;ailleurs de la région.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Aujourd&#039;hui, il est possible de voir de nombreux vestiges des périodes islamiques anciennes et médiévales en Jordanie. De nombreuses ruines historiques, telles que des châteaux, des forts, des tours, des thermes, des auberges pour caravanes et des palais fortifiés, parsèment le terrain en forme de steppe de l&#039;est de la Jordanie et les collines centrales. Connus collectivement sous le nom de châteaux ou palais du désert, ils faisaient à l&#039;origine partie d&#039;une chaîne s&#039;étendant du nord de Damas jusqu&#039;à Khirbet al-Mafjar, près d&#039;Ariha (ou Jéricho).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;fr/qasr-al-kharanah/&quot;&gt;Qasr Al-Kharanah&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;en/qasr-amra/&quot;&gt;Qasr Amra&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Desert Castles/qasr-amra.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3202.960326365759!2d36.46056488753891!3d31.7285686252473!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b249e0321d58d:0xae2394f52625c2b!2sQasr al-Kharaneh!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569247005481!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 395, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'les-chateaux-du-desert'),
(397, 'Castelli nel Deserto', 'Castelli nel Deserto', 'Allungando verso est di Amman, la pianura arida del deserto rotola verso l&#039;Iraq e l&#039;Arabia Saudita.', 'Allungando verso est di Amman, la pianura arida del deserto rotola verso l&#039;Iraq e l&#039;Arabia Saudita.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Allungando verso est di Amman, la pianura arida del deserto rotola verso l&#039;Iraq e l&#039;Arabia Saudita. Questo è un luogo in cui sabbia infinita e paesaggi di basalto sterile dimostrano la capacità dell&#039;uomo di prosperare in condizioni difficili.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La scoperta di assi di selce in questo deserto indica che i coloni paleolitici abitavano la regione circa mezzo milione di anni fa. Ma i resti più notevoli dell&#039;abitazione umana sono i palazzi costruiti dai califfi omayyadi di Damasco durante i primi giorni dell&#039;Islam (VII-VIII secolo d.C.).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Al culmine della dinastia omayyade, l&#039;architettura fiorì con lo scambio culturale che accompagnava le rotte commerciali in crescita. Nel 750 d.C., quando la dinastia omayyade fu rovesciata dagli Abbasidi di Baghdad, un&#039;architettura musulmana riccamente caratteristica si stava evolvendo, grazie all&#039;influenza cosmopolita di costruttori e artigiani attirati dall&#039;Egitto, dalla Mesopotamia e da altre parti della regione.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Oggi è possibile vedere molte reliquie del periodo islamico antico e medievale in Giordania. Sparsi in tutto il terreno simile alla steppa della Giordania orientale e le colline centrali sono numerose rovine storiche, tra cui castelli, fortezze, torri, bagni, locande per roulotte e palazzi fortificati. Conosciuti collettivamente come castelli del deserto o palazzi del deserto, originariamente facevano parte di una catena che si estendeva da nord di Damasco fino a Khirbet al-Mafjar, vicino ad Ariha (o Gerico).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;it/qasr-al-kharanah/&quot;&gt;Qasr Al-Kharanah&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;it/qasr-amra/&quot;&gt;Qasr Amra&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Desert Castles/qasr-amra.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3202.960326365759!2d36.46056488753891!3d31.7285686252473!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b249e0321d58d:0xae2394f52625c2b!2sQasr al-Kharaneh!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569247005481!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 395, 'it', '', 'one col', 'castelli-nel-deserto'),
(398, 'Madaba', 'Madaba', 'Madaba is best known for its Byzantine and Umayyad mosaics, especially a large Byzantine-era mosaic map of the Holy Land.', 'Madaba is best known for its Byzantine and Umayyad mosaics, especially a large Byzantine-era mosaic map of the Holy Land.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Madaba is the capital city of Madaba Governorate in central Jordan, with a population of about 60,000. It is best known for its Byzantine and Umayyad mosaics, especially a large Byzantine-Era mosaic map of the Holy Land. Madaba is located 30 kilometres (19 miles) south-west of the capital Amman.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The town of Madaba was once a Moabite border city, mentioned in the Bible. Madaba dates from the Middle Bronze Age. During its rule by the Roman and Byzantine empires from the 2nd to the 7th centuries, the city formed part of the Provincia Arabia set up by the Roman Emperor Trajan to replace the Nabataean kingdom of Petra.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The main sites of Madaba:&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Church of Saint George which houses the famous Map of Madaba that was discovered in 1896 a mosaic of the 6th century representing a map of the Holy Land, sometimes called the &quot;Church of the Map&quot;. With two million pieces of colored stone, the map depicts hills, valleys and villages. (Entrance 1 JOD, not included in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Church of the Apostles, the ruins of this Byzantine church date to 578 CE, and are currently being restored. It includes a mosaic known as the &quot;Personification of the Sea&quot;, depicting a woman emerging from the sea, surrounded by mythical aquatic creatures and a hodgepodge of rams, bulls, parrots and exotic vegetation. The mosaic was signed by a mosaicist named Salamanios. (included in &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;St. John the Baptist Roman Catholic Church offers a magnificent view of the city as it is possible to climb up to the top of the bell tower (ticket, not included in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The city is rather nice and in addition to the visits of churches, it is quite pleasant to stroll around the city and nibble something in one the several traditional restaurants in the town.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Madaba/madaba mosque.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d54304.0835391128!2d35.7633807408465!3d31.71575236400819!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151cacd00bad3bc5:0x4d6d5834c1003e2b!2sMadaba!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564829017080!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 398, 'en', '', 'one col', 'madaba');
INSERT INTO `en33_pages` (`id`, `name`, `title`, `meta_desc`, `meta_key`, `contents`, `published`, `lang_id`, `lang`, `icon`, `layout`, `url`) VALUES
(399, 'Madaba', 'Madaba', 'Madaba est la capitale du gouvernorat de Madaba, au centre de la Jordanie, et compte environ 60 000 habitants. Il est surtout connu pour ses mosaïques byzantines et omeyyades,', 'Madaba est la capitale du gouvernorat de Madaba, au centre de la Jordanie, et compte environ 60 000 habitants. Il est surtout connu pour ses mosaïques byzantines et omeyyades,', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Madaba est la capitale du gouvernorat de Madaba, au centre de la Jordanie, et compte environ 60 000 habitants. Il est surtout connu pour ses mosaïques byzantines et omeyyades, en particulier pour sa grande carte mosaïque d’époque byzantine-ère de la Terre Sainte. Madaba est située à 30 kilomètres au sud-ouest de la capitale, Amman.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La ville de Madaba était autrefois une ville frontière mabite, mentionnée dans la Bible. Madaba date de l&#039;âge du bronze moyen. Au cours de son règne par les empires romain et byzantin du IIe au VIIe siècle, la ville faisait partie de la Provincia Arabia créée par l&#039;empereur romain Trajan pour remplacer le royaume nabatéen de Pétra.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Les principaux sites de Madaba:&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;L&#039;église Saint-Georges qui abrite la célèbre carte de Madaba découverte en 1896, une mosaïque du VIe siècle représentant une carte de la Terre Sainte, parfois appelée &quot;l&#039;église de la carte&quot;. Avec deux millions de morceaux de pierre colorée, la carte représente des collines, des vallées et des villages. (Entrée 1 JOD, non incluse dans le &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Eglise des Apôtres, les ruines de cette église byzantine datent de 578 de notre ère et sont en cours de restauration. Il comprend une mosaïque connue sous le nom de &quot;personnification de la mer&quot;, représentant une femme émergeant de la mer, entourée de créatures aquatiques mythiques et d’un mélange de béliers, taureaux, perroquets et végétation exotique. La mosaïque a été signée par un mosaïste nommé Salamanios. (inclus dans le &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;L&#039;église de San Giovanni Battista (église du décollage de Giovanni Battista) qui offre une vue magnifique sur la ville car il est possible de monter au sommet du clocher (billet, non inclus dans le &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La ville est plutôt agréable et, en plus des visites d’églises, il est agréable de se promener et de grignoter quelque chose dans l’un des nombreux restaurants traditionnels de la ville.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;<br><br>&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Madaba/madaba mosque.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d54304.0835391128!2d35.7633807408465!3d31.71575236400819!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151cacd00bad3bc5:0x4d6d5834c1003e2b!2sMadaba!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564829017080!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 398, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'madaba'),
(400, 'Madaba', 'Madaba', 'Madaba è la capitale del Governatorato di Madaba nella Giordania centrale, con una popolazione di circa 60.000 abitanti.', 'Madaba è la capitale del Governatorato di Madaba nella Giordania centrale, con una popolazione di circa 60.000 abitanti.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Madaba è la capitale del Governatorato di Madaba nella Giordania centrale, con una popolazione di circa 60.000 abitanti. È meglio noto per i suoi mosaici bizantini e omayyadi, in particolare una grande mappa a mosaico dell&#039;era bizantina della Terra Santa. Madaba si trova a 30 chilometri (19 miglia) a sud-ovest della capitale Amman.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La città di Madaba era una volta una città di confine moabita, menzionata nella Bibbia. Madaba risale alla media età del bronzo. Durante il suo dominio da parte degli imperi romano e bizantino dal 2 ° al 7 ° secolo, la città faceva parte della Provincia Arabia istituita dall&#039;imperatore romano Traiano per sostituire il regno nabateo di Petra.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;I principali siti di Madaba:&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Chiesa di San Giorgio che ospita la famosa Mappa di Madaba che fu scoperta nel 1896 un mosaico del VI secolo che rappresentava una mappa di Terra Santa, a volte chiamata &quot;Chiesa della Mappa&quot;. Con due milioni di pezzi di pietra colorata, la mappa raffigura colline, vallate e villaggi. (Ingresso 1 JOD, non incluso nel Jordan Pass)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Chiesa degli Apostoli, le rovine di questa chiesa bizantina risalgono al 578 d.C. e sono attualmente in fase di restauro. Include un mosaico noto come &quot;Personificazione del mare&quot;, raffigurante una donna che emerge dal mare, circondata da mitiche creature acquatiche e un miscuglio di arieti, tori, pappagalli e vegetazione esotica. Il mosaico è stato firmato da un mosaicista di nome Salamanios. (incluso nel Jordan Pass)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Chiesa di San Giovanni Battista (Chiesa del decollo di Giovanni Battista) che offre una magnifica vista della città in quanto è possibile salire fino alla cima del campanile (biglietto, non incluso nel Jordan Pass)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La città è piuttosto bella e oltre alle visite delle chiese, è abbastanza piacevole passeggiare per la città e sgranocchiare qualcosa in uno dei numerosi ristoranti tradizionali della città.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Madaba/madaba mosque.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d54304.0835391128!2d35.7633807408465!3d31.71575236400819!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151cacd00bad3bc5:0x4d6d5834c1003e2b!2sMadaba!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564829017080!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 398, 'it', '', 'one col', 'madaba'),
(401, 'Mount Nebo', 'Mount Nebo', 'Mount Nebo is one of the biblical sites that can be seen during a trip to Jordan.', 'Mount Nebo', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Mount Nebo is one of the biblical sites that can be seen during your trip to Jordan.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;According to the Bible, it was from Mount Nebo that Moses contemplated the Promised Land after God forbade him to enter. Moreover, for Christians, it is on this mountain where the tomb of Moses is. For Muslims, it would be in Nabi Musa, on the other side of the Jordan, in Palestine.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;As part of the attractions of this magnificent place you will see:&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;The Serpentine Cross of Moses (The Brazen Serpent Monument)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Remains of the Basilica of Moses &lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;About 1 km East of Mount Nebo, you can see the springs of Moses (Ayun Musa), are a collection of fresh water springs said to be where Moses during the Exodus was directed by God to throw a tree branch, possibly a barberry into the bitter springs to make them sweet enough to drink.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Near Mount Nebo is the village of Khirbet al-Mukkhayat. The village is known for hosting numerous Byzantine remains including mosaics found in the chapel of the priest John and the church of Saints.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;<br><br>&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Mount_nebo/Monte-nebo.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d13568.31599039157!2d35.71652272680265!3d31.768331250610355!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151cad7ed4c82179:0x131a1cf280726293!2sMount+Nebo!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564830031400!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 401, 'en', '', 'one col', 'mount-nebo'),
(402, 'Mont Nebo', 'Mont Nebo', 'Mount Nebo est l&#039;un des sites bibliques à découvrir lors de votre voyage en Jordanie.', 'Mount Nebo est l&#039;un des sites bibliques à découvrir lors de votre voyage en Jordanie.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Mont Nebo est l&#039;un des sites bibliques à découvrir lors de votre voyage en Jordanie.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Selon la Bible, c&#039;est du mont Nebo que Moïse a contemplé la Terre promise après que Dieu lui ait interdit d&#039;entrer. De plus, pour les chrétiens, c&#039;est sur cette montagne que se trouve le tombeau de Moïse. Pour les musulmans, ce serait à Nabi Musa, de l&#039;autre côté du Jourdain, en Palestine.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Dans le cadre des attractions de ce lieu magnifique, vous verrez:&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Croix serpentine de Moïse (Monument au serpent d&#039;airain)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Vestiges de la basilique de Moïse&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;À environ 1 km à l&#039;est du mont Nebo, vous pouvez voir les sources de Moïse (Ayun Musa). Il s&#039;agit d&#039;une collection de sources d&#039;eau douce considérées comme étant l&#039;endroit où Moïse avait été ordonné par Dieu de lancer une branche d&#039;arbre, éventuellement un sources amères pour les rendre assez sucrés pour boire.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Près du mont Nebo se trouve le village de Khirbet al-Mukkhayat. Le village est connu pour abriter de nombreux vestiges byzantins, notamment des mosaïques trouvées dans la chapelle du prêtre Jean et dans l&#039;église des Saints.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Mount_nebo/Monte-nebo.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d13568.31599039157!2d35.71652272680265!3d31.768331250610355!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151cad7ed4c82179:0x131a1cf280726293!2sMount+Nebo!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564830031400!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 401, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'mont-nebo'),
(403, 'Monte Nebo', 'Monte Nebo', 'Il Monte Nebo è uno dei siti biblici che possono essere visti durante il tuo viaggio in Giordania.', 'Il Monte Nebo è uno dei siti biblici che possono essere visti durante il tuo viaggio in Giordania.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Il Monte Nebo è uno dei siti biblici che possono essere visti durante il tuo viaggio in Giordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Secondo la Bibbia, fu dal Monte Nebo che Mosè contemplò la Terra Promessa dopo che Dio gli proibì di entrare. Inoltre, per i cristiani, è su questa montagna dove si trova la tomba di Mosè. Per i musulmani, sarebbe a Nabi Musa, dall&#039;altra parte del Giordano, in Palestina.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Come parte delle attrazioni di questo magnifico luogo vedrai:&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;La Serpentine Cross of Moses (The Brazen Serpent Monument)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Resti della Basilica di Mosè&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;A circa 1 km a est del Monte Nebo, puoi vedere le sorgenti di Mosè (Ayun Musa), sono una raccolta di sorgenti d&#039;acqua dolce che si dice essere dove Mosè durante l&#039;Esodo fu diretto da Dio a lanciare un ramo di un albero, forse un crespino nel molle amare per renderle abbastanza dolci da bere.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Vicino al monte Nebo si trova il villaggio di Khirbet al-Mukkhayat. Il villaggio è noto per ospitare numerosi resti bizantini tra cui mosaici trovati nella cappella del sacerdote Giovanni e nella chiesa dei Santi.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Mount_nebo/Monte-nebo.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d13568.31599039157!2d35.71652272680265!3d31.768331250610355!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151cad7ed4c82179:0x131a1cf280726293!2sMount+Nebo!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564830031400!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 401, 'it', '', 'one col', 'mount-nebo'),
(404, 'The Dead Sea', 'The Dead Sea', 'The Dead Sea is one of the most spectacular natural and spiritual landscapes in the whole World.', 'The Dead Sea', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The Dead Sea is a salt lake bordered by Jordan to the East and Israel and the West Bank to the West. It lies in the Jordan Rift Valley, and the Jordan River is the only major water source flowing into the Dead Sea.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Its surface and shores are 430.5 meters (1,412 ft) below sea level, Earth&#039;s lowest elevation on land. 9.6 times as salty as the ocean water, it is one of the world&#039;s saltiest bodies of water; because its salinity you can float in the Dead Sea without even trying, which makes swimming here a truly unique experience not to be missed. This unique place has extremely high content of salts and minerals which gives its waters the curative powers and therapeutic qualities recognized for more than 2000 years ago.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Nowadays visitors from all over the World go to the Dead Sea to treat various health problems such as Psoriasis, the Climatotherapy at the Dead Sea may be a therapy for psoriasis by sunbathing for long periods in the area due to its position below sea level and subsequent result that UV rays are partially blocked by the increased cloud cover. Rhinosinusitis patients receiving Dead Sea saline nasal irrigation exhibited improved symptom relief compared to standard hypertonic saline spray and Osteoarthritis, Dead Sea mud pack therapy has been suggested to temporarily relieve pain in patients with osteoarthritis of the knees,  treatment with mineral-rich mud compresses can be used to augment conventional medical therapy.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The Dead Sea is one of the most spectacular natural and spiritual landscapes in the whole World; there is much to do on the shores of the Dead Sea, you will be delighted.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Deadsea/Dead Sea website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d435268.73507000995!2d35.21009266120768!3d31.536874322287797!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15033c2eaf9fbba1:0xf38cff48a0c15882!2sDead+Sea!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564839572942!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 404, 'en', '', 'one col', 'the-dead-sea'),
(405, 'La Mer Morte', 'La Mer Morte', 'La mer Morte est un lac salé bordé par la Jordanie à l&#039;est, Israël et la Cisjordanie à l&#039;ouest. Il se situe dans la vallée du Jourdain, et le Jourdain est la seule source d’eau majeure se déversant dans la mer Morte.', 'La mer Morte est un lac salé bordé par la Jordanie à l&#039;est, Israël et la Cisjordanie à l&#039;ouest. Il se situe dans la vallée du Jourdain, et le Jourdain est la seule source d’eau majeure se déversant dans la mer Morte.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La mer Morte est un lac salé bordé par la Jordanie à l&#039;est, Israël et la Cisjordanie à l&#039;ouest. Il se situe dans la vallée du Jourdain, et le Jourdain est la seule source d’eau majeure se déversant dans la mer Morte.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Sa surface et ses rives sont à 430,5 mètres au-dessous du niveau de la mer, l&#039;altitude la plus basse de la Terre. 9,6 fois plus salée que l&#039;eau de l&#039;océan, c&#039;est l&#039;une des eaux les plus salées au monde; parce que sa salinité permet de flotter dans la mer Morte sans même essayer, ce qui fait de la baignade une expérience unique à ne pas manquer. Cet endroit unique possède une teneur extrêmement élevée en sels et minéraux qui lui confère les pouvoirs curatifs et les qualités thérapeutiques reconnues depuis plus de 2000 ans.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;De nos jours, des visiteurs du monde entier se rendent dans la mer Morte pour traiter divers problèmes de santé, tels que le psoriasis. La climatothérapie à la mer Morte peut être une thérapie du psoriasis par un bronzage prolongé dans la région en raison de sa position en dessous du niveau de la mer Il en résulte que les rayons UV sont partiellement bloqués par l’augmentation de la couverture nuageuse. Les patients atteints de rhinosinusite recevant une irrigation saline saline de la Mer Morte ont montré un soulagement amélioré des symptômes par rapport au spray salin hypertonique standard et à l’arthrose, il a été suggéré que le traitement par une compresse de boue de la Mer Morte soulage temporairement la douleur utilisé pour augmenter le traitement médical conventionnel.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La mer Morte est l&#039;un des paysages naturels et spirituels les plus spectaculaires du monde entier; il y a beaucoup à faire sur les rives de la mer Morte, vous serez ravis.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Deadsea/Dead Sea website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d435268.73507000995!2d35.21009266120768!3d31.536874322287797!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15033c2eaf9fbba1:0xf38cff48a0c15882!2sDead+Sea!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564839572942!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 404, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'la-mer-morte'),
(406, 'IL Mar Morto', 'IL Mar Morto', 'Il Mar Morto è un lago salato delimitato dalla Giordania ad est e da Israele e dalla Cisgiordania ad ovest.', 'Il Mar Morto è un lago salato delimitato dalla Giordania ad est e da Israele e dalla Cisgiordania ad ovest.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Il Mar Morto è un lago salato delimitato dalla Giordania ad est e da Israele e dalla Cisgiordania ad ovest. Si trova nella Jordan Rift Valley e il fiume Giordano è l&#039;unica grande fonte d&#039;acqua che sfocia nel Mar Morto.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La sua superficie e le sue rive sono 430,5 metri (1.412 piedi) sotto il livello del mare, la più bassa altitudine della Terra sulla terra. 9,6 volte più salato dell&#039;acqua dell&#039;oceano, è uno dei corpi idrici più salati del mondo; grazie alla sua salinità puoi galleggiare nel Mar Morto senza nemmeno provarci, il che rende il nuoto qui un&#039;esperienza davvero unica da non perdere. Questo luogo unico ha un contenuto estremamente elevato di sali e minerali che conferisce alle sue acque i poteri curativi e le qualità terapeutiche riconosciute più di 2000 anni fa.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Oggi i visitatori di tutto il mondo vanno nel Mar Morto per curare vari problemi di salute come la psoriasi, la climatoterapia nel Mar Morto può essere una terapia per la psoriasi prendendo il sole per lunghi periodi nell&#039;area a causa della sua posizione sotto il livello del mare e successive risulta che i raggi UV sono parzialmente bloccati dall&#039;aumentata copertura nuvolosa. I pazienti affetti da rinosinusite che ricevono irrigazione nasale salina del Mar Morto hanno mostrato un miglioramento dei sintomi rispetto allo spray salino ipertonico standard e all&#039;osteoartrite, è stata suggerita la terapia con impacchi di fango del Mar Morto per alleviare temporaneamente il dolore nei pazienti con osteoartrosi delle ginocchia, il trattamento con impacchi di fango ricchi di minerali può essere utilizzato per aumentare la terapia medica convenzionale.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Il Mar Morto è uno dei paesaggi naturali e spirituali più spettacolari di tutto il mondo; c&#039;è molto da fare sulle rive del Mar Morto, ne rimarrai deliziato.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Deadsea/Dead Sea website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d435268.73507000995!2d35.21009266120768!3d31.536874322287797!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15033c2eaf9fbba1:0xf38cff48a0c15882!2sDead+Sea!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564839572942!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 404, 'it', '', 'one col', 'il-mar-morto'),
(407, 'Ajloun', 'Ajloun', 'Travelling north of Jordan, Ajloun and its Castle is definitely worth a visit. The hills and green spaces are unparalleled.', 'Travelling north of Jordan, Ajloun and its Castle is definitely worth a visit. The hills and green spaces are unparalleled.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Travelling north of Jordan, Ajloun and its Castle definitely worth a visit. Ajlun, is the capital town of the Ajloun Governorate, a hilly town in the north of Jordan, located 76 kilometers (around 47 miles) north west of Amman. It is noted for its impressive ruins of the 12th-century Ajloun Castle. This place winds through fertile green hills lined with olive groves.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Ajlun Castle is located on the site of an old monastery. It was renovated as a fort in 1184 by Izz al-Din Usama, a general in the army of Saladin. The castle controlled traffic along the road connecting Damascus and Egypt. The fortress marks the furthest limit of Frankish incursions during the Crusades.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Some of the stones with which the castle was built have crosses carved into them, giving credence to a tradition, recounted by a 13th century Arab historian that: &quot;an ancient monastery once stood on the site, inhabited by a Christian named Ajloun; when the monastery fell into ruin, the castle took its place and the name of the monk&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Located in the center of Ajloun is the Great Ajlun Mosque. This mosque is one of the oldest extant in Jordan and dates back around 800 years. This edifice was previously a Byzantine Christian church; there have been reports of Greek writing in the oldest sections. The prayer tower is called &quot;the filter&quot; by some locals (referring to a cigarette filter, because half of the tower was built over a square tower, most likely a Church bell tower).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;This place will captivate you for sure.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Ajlun/Ajloun website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d53934.297894855255!2d35.7322292455951!3d32.34156536287274!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151c87da460049bd:0x3fbf8443e03b269a!2sAjloun!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564839902477!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 407, 'en', '', 'one col', 'ajloun'),
(408, 'Ajloun', 'Ajloun', 'Voyageant au nord de la Jordanie, Ajloun et son château valent vraiment une visite. Ajlun est la capitale du gouvernorat d&#039;Ajloun, une ville vallonnée du nord de la Jordanie', 'Voyageant au nord de la Jordanie, Ajloun et son château valent vraiment une visite. Ajlun est la capitale du gouvernorat d&#039;Ajloun, une ville vallonnée du nord de la Jordanie', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Voyageant au nord de la Jordanie, Ajloun et son château valent vraiment une visite. Ajlun est la capitale du gouvernorat d&#039;Ajloun, une ville vallonnée du nord de la Jordanie, située à 76 kilomètres au nord-ouest d&#039;Amman. Il est connu pour ses impressionnantes ruines du château d&#039;Ajloun, datant du XIIe siècle. Cet endroit serpente à travers des collines verdoyantes et fertiles bordées d&#039;oliveraies.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Le château d&#039;Ajlun est situé sur le site d&#039;un ancien monastère. Il fut transformé en fort en 1184 par Izz al-Din Usama, général de l&#039;armée de Saladin. Le château contrôlait la circulation le long de la route reliant Damas et l’Égypte. La forteresse marque la limite ultime des incursions franches lors des croisades.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Des croix ont été gravées sur certaines des pierres avec lesquelles le château a été construit, ce qui témoigne d&#039;une tradition racontée par un historien arabe du XIIIe siècle: le monastère est tombé en ruine, le château a pris sa place et le nom du moine &quot;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La Grande Mosquée Ajlun est située dans le centre d&#039;Ajloun. Cette mosquée est l’une des plus anciennes de Jordanie et remonte à environ 800 ans. Cet édifice était auparavant une église chrétienne byzantine; des écrits en grec ont été rapportés dans les sections les plus anciennes. La tour de prière est appelée &quot;le filtre&quot; par certains habitants (en référence à un filtre de cigarette, car la moitié de la tour a été construite sur une tour carrée, très probablement un clocher de l&#039;église).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Cet endroit vous captivera à coup sûr.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Ajlun/Ajloun website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d53934.297894855255!2d35.7322292455951!3d32.34156536287274!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151c87da460049bd:0x3fbf8443e03b269a!2sAjloun!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564839902477!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 407, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'ajloun'),
(409, 'Ajloun', 'Ajloun', 'Viaggiando a nord della Giordania, Ajloun e il suo castello meritano sicuramente una visita. Ajlun, è la capitale del Governatorato di Ajloun,', 'Viaggiando a nord della Giordania, Ajloun e il suo castello meritano sicuramente una visita. Ajlun, è la capitale del Governatorato di Ajloun,', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Viaggiando a nord della Giordania, Ajloun e il suo castello meritano sicuramente una visita. Ajlun, è la capitale del Governatorato di Ajloun, una città collinare nel nord della Giordania, situata a 76 chilometri (circa 47 miglia) a nord ovest di Amman. È noto per le sue imponenti rovine del castello Ajloun del XII secolo. Questo luogo si snoda attraverso fertili colline verdi fiancheggiate da uliveti.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Il castello di Ajlun si trova sul sito di un antico monastero. Fu rinnovato come fortezza nel 1184 da Izz al-Din Usama, un generale dell&#039;esercito di Saladino. Il castello controllava il traffico lungo la strada che collegava Damasco e l&#039;Egitto. La fortezza segna il limite più lontano delle incursioni dei Franchi durante le Crociate.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Alcune delle pietre con cui è stato costruito il castello hanno croci incise su di esse, dando credito a una tradizione, raccontata da uno storico arabo del 13 ° secolo che: &quot;un antico monastero sorgeva sul sito, abitato da un cristiano di nome Ajloun; quando il il monastero cadde in rovina, il castello prese il suo posto e il nome del monaco &quot;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Nel centro di Ajloun si trova la Grande Moschea Ajlun. Questa moschea è una delle più antiche esistenti in Giordania e risale a circa 800 anni fa. Questo edificio era precedentemente una chiesa cristiana bizantina; ci sono stati rapporti di scrittura greca nelle sezioni più antiche. La torre di preghiera è chiamata &quot;il filtro&quot; da alcuni locali (riferendosi a un filtro per sigarette, perché metà della torre era costruita su una torre quadrata, molto probabilmente un campanile della Chiesa).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Questo posto ti conquisterà di sicuro.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Ajlun/Ajloun website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d53934.297894855255!2d35.7322292455951!3d32.34156536287274!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151c87da460049bd:0x3fbf8443e03b269a!2sAjloun!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564839902477!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 407, 'it', '', 'one col', 'ajloun'),
(410, 'Little Petra', 'Little Petra', 'Little Petra is also known in Arabic as Siq al-Barid &quot;the cold canyon&quot;. Like Petra, it is a Nabataean site, with buildings carved into the walls of the sandstone canyons.', 'Little Petra is also known in Arabic as Siq al-Barid &quot;the cold canyon&quot;. Like Petra, it is a Nabataean site, with buildings carved into the walls of the sandstone canyons.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Little Petra is also known in Arabic as Siq al-Barid &quot;the cold canyon&quot;, comes from its orientation and its high walls preventing the entry of most available sunlight. It is an archaeological site located north of Petra and the town of Wadi Musa in the Ma&#039;an Governorate of Jordan. Like Petra, it is a Nabataean site and as its name suggests it is much smaller than Petra; however, is crammed with tombs, temples, triclinium or dining room, houses, water channels and cisterns carved into the walls of the sandstone canyons.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Little Petra is part of the Petra Archeological Park, though accessed separately, and included in Petra&#039;s inscription as a UNESCO World Heritage Site.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Like Petra, Little Petra is open to the public during the daytime. It is, however, operated separately, and does not require an admission ticket and fee as Petra does. The local Bedouins sell souvenirs and snacks in the small parking lot. Many visitors to Petra have increasingly been including Little Petra on their itineraries. Guidebooks recommend it as less crowded and more relaxed than Petra itself. The Painted House, which has no counterpart at Petra, has also added to the attraction.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;At the west end of the canyon a set of steps leads to the top of the rock at this point a Bedouin has installed a nice tearoom so you can enjoy the stunning view. It is also possible to hike via the 6-kilometre (3.7 mi) trail from the end of the canyon that unites Little Petra to Petra´s Monastery known in Arabic as Ad Deir. Those who make the journey are advised to do so with a guide as the trail, while obvious in many places, is not formally marked. Hikers are also cautioned against attempting the trail alone, or late in the day, as nights in the region are often cold. It is also forbidden to enter Petra without having paid the site&#039;s admission.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Petra/Little Petra 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3442.1499734441923!2d35.44871971471867!3d30.37509898176327!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15016f643bc2d24b:0xafd3ecb219086144!2sTriclinium!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564842717941!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 410, 'en', '', 'one col', 'little-petra'),
(411, 'Little Petra', 'Little Petra', 'La petite Petra est également connue en arabe sous le nom de Siq al-Barid, &quot;le canyon froid&quot;,', 'La petite Petra est également connue en arabe sous le nom de Siq al-Barid, &quot;le canyon froid&quot;,', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La petite Petra est également connue en arabe sous le nom de Siq al-Barid, &quot;le canyon froid&quot;, en raison de son orientation et de ses hauts murs qui empêchent la lumière du soleil de pénétrer à fond. Il s’agit d’un site archéologique situé au nord de Petra et de la ville de Wadi Musa dans le gouvernorat de Ma&#039;an en Jordanie. Comme Petra, il s’agit d’un site nabatéen et, comme son nom l’indique, il est beaucoup plus petit que Petra; Cependant, il est rempli de tombes, de temples, de triclinium ou de salle à manger, de maisons, de canaux d’eau et de citernes creusées dans les murs des canyons de grès.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Little Petra fait partie du parc archéologique de Petra, bien que accessible séparément et incluse dans l&#039;inscription de Petra en tant que site du patrimoine mondial de l&#039;UNESCO.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Comme Petra, Little Petra est ouverte au public pendant la journée. Il est cependant exploité séparément et ne nécessite pas d’entrée ni de frais d’entrée, contrairement à Petra. Les bédouins locaux vendent des souvenirs et des collations dans le petit parking. De nombreux visiteurs à Petra ont de plus en plus inclus Little Petra sur leurs itinéraires. Les guides le recommandent comme étant moins encombré et plus détendu que Petra. La Painted House, qui n&#039;a pas d&#039;équivalent à Pétra, a également contribué à l&#039;attraction.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;À l&#039;extrémité ouest du canyon, un ensemble d&#039;escaliers mène au sommet du rocher. À ce stade, un Bédouin a installé un joli salon de thé afin que vous puissiez profiter d&#039;une vue imprenable. Il est également possible de faire de la randonnée sur le sentier de 6 km (6 km) qui part du bout du canyon qui unit Little Petra au monastère de Petra, connu en arabe sous le nom de Ad Deir. Ceux qui font le voyage sont invités à le faire avec un guide car le sentier, bien qu&#039;évident dans de nombreux endroits, n&#039;est pas officiellement indiqué. Les randonneurs sont également avertis de ne pas tenter le sentier seul ou en fin de journée, car les nuits dans la région sont souvent froides. Il est également interdit d&#039;entrer dans Petra sans avoir payé l&#039;entrée du site.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Petra/Little Petra 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3442.1499734441923!2d35.44871971471867!3d30.37509898176327!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15016f643bc2d24b:0xafd3ecb219086144!2sTriclinium!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564842717941!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 410, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'little-petra'),
(412, 'Little Petra', 'Little Petra', 'Little Petra è anche conosciuto in arabo come Siq al-Barid &quot;il canyon freddo&quot;, deriva dal suo orientamento e dalle sue alte mura che impediscono', 'Little Petra è anche conosciuto in arabo come Siq al-Barid &quot;il canyon freddo&quot;, deriva dal suo orientamento e dalle sue alte mura che impediscono', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Little Petra è anche conosciuto in arabo come Siq al-Barid &quot;il canyon freddo&quot;, deriva dal suo orientamento e dalle sue alte mura che impediscono l&#039;ingresso della maggior parte della luce solare disponibile. È un sito archeologico situato a nord di Petra e la città di Wadi Musa nel Governatorato di Ma&#039;an in Giordania. Come Petra, è un sito nabateo e come suggerisce il nome è molto più piccolo di Petra; tuttavia, è pieno zeppo di tombe, templi, triclinio o sala da pranzo, case, canali d&#039;acqua e cisterne scolpite nelle pareti dei canyon di arenaria.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Little Petra fa parte del Parco archeologico di Petra, anche se accessibile separatamente, ed è inclusa nell&#039;iscrizione di Petra come patrimonio mondiale dell&#039;UNESCO.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Come Petra, Little Petra è aperta al pubblico durante il giorno. Tuttavia, è gestito separatamente e non richiede un biglietto di ingresso e una tassa come Petra. I beduini locali vendono souvenir e snack nel piccolo parcheggio. Molti visitatori di Petra hanno incluso sempre più Little Petra nei loro itinerari. Le guide lo raccomandano come meno affollato e più rilassato della stessa Petra. Anche la Painted House, che non ha controparti a Petra, ha aggiunto all&#039;attrazione.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;All&#039;estremità occidentale del canyon una serie di gradini conduce alla cima della roccia a questo punto un beduino ha installato una bella sala da tè in modo da poter godere di una vista mozzafiato. È anche possibile fare un&#039;escursione attraverso il sentiero di 6 chilometri (3,7 miglia) dalla fine del canyon che unisce Little Petra al monastero di Petra, noto in arabo come Ad Deir. Si consiglia a coloro che effettuano il viaggio di farlo con una guida poiché il sentiero, sebbene evidente in molti luoghi, non è formalmente segnato. Gli escursionisti sono anche avvertiti di non tentare il sentiero da soli o nel corso della giornata, poiché le notti nella regione sono spesso fredde. È inoltre vietato entrare a Petra senza aver pagato l&#039;ammissione del sito.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Petra/Little Petra 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3442.1499734441923!2d35.44871971471867!3d30.37509898176327!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15016f643bc2d24b:0xafd3ecb219086144!2sTriclinium!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564842717941!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 410, 'it', '', 'one col', 'little-petra'),
(413, 'Petra', 'Petra', 'Undoubtedly the most famous attraction in Jordan is the Nabataean city of Petra, nestled away in the mountains south of the Dead Sea. Petra, which means &quot;stone&quot; in Greek', 'Undoubtedly the most famous attraction in Jordan is the Nabataean city of Petra, nestled away in the mountains south of the Dead Sea. Petra, which means &quot;stone&quot; in Greek', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Undoubtedly the symbol of Jordan, the most famous and visited attraction is the Nabatean city of Petra, nestled away in the mountains south of the Dead Sea. Petra, means &quot;stone&quot; in Greek, is perhaps the most spectacular ancient city remaining in the modern world.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Petra has been a UNESCO World Heritage site since 1985 and one of the New 7 Wonders of the World that enchants visitors from all corners of the Globe. UNESCO has described it as &quot;one of the most precious cultural properties of man&#039;s cultural heritage&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The city was the capital of the Nabataeans. Arabs who settled and dominated in southern Jordan for more than 2000 years ago during pre-Roman times. They were particularly skillful in harvesting rainwater, agriculture and carved this wonderland of temples, tombs and elaborate buildings out of solid rock. Petra flourished in the 1st century AD, when its famous Khazneh or The Treasury structure – believed to be the mausoleum of Nabataean king Aretas IV – was constructed, and its population peaked at an estimated 20,000 inhabitants&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The victorian traveler and poet Dean Burgon gave Petra a description which holds to this day -&quot;Match me such a marvel save in Eastern clime, a rose-red city half as old as time.&quot;  &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Yet words can hardly do justice to the magnificence that is Petra. In order to best savor the atmosphere of this ancient wonder, visit in the quiet of the early morning or late afternoon when the sandstone rock glows red with quiet grandeur. It is certainly a must-see for visitors to Jordan and the Middle East.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Petra/khazna4.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d13776.124196576167!2d35.471370226142305!3d30.321634658514736!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15016930021ab6b1:0xe43a697bc3a3e0b9!2sWadi+Musa!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564843293999!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 413, 'en', '', 'one col', 'petra'),
(414, 'Petra', 'Petra', 'Sans aucun doute le symbole de la Jordanie, l&#039;attraction la plus célèbre et la plus visitée est la ville nabatéenne de Petra, située dans les montagnes au sud de la mer Morte. Petra, qui signifie «pierre» en grec', 'Sans aucun doute le symbole de la Jordanie, l&#039;attraction la plus célèbre et la plus visitée est la ville nabatéenne de Petra, située dans les montagnes au sud de la mer Morte. Petra, qui signifie «pierre» en grec', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Sans aucun doute le symbole de la Jordanie, l&#039;attraction la plus célèbre et la plus visitée est la ville nabatéenne de Petra, située dans les montagnes au sud de la mer Morte. Petra, qui signifie «pierre» en grec, est peut-être la plus ancienne ville la plus spectaculaire du monde moderne.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Petra est inscrite au patrimoine mondial de l’UNESCO depuis 1985 et est l’une des 7 nouvelles merveilles du monde qui enchante les visiteurs du monde entier. L&#039;UNESCO l&#039;a décrite comme &quot;l&#039;un des biens culturels les plus précieux du patrimoine culturel de l&#039;homme&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La ville était la capitale des Nabatéens. Les Arabes qui se sont installés et ont dominé le sud de la Jordanie pendant plus de 2000 ans au cours de l&#039;ère pré-romaine. Ils étaient particulièrement habiles à collecter l&#039;eau de pluie et l&#039;agriculture, et sculptèrent ces terres merveilleuses de temples, de tombeaux et d&#039;édifices en pierre solide. Petra a prospéré au 1er siècle de notre ère. C., lors de la construction de sa célèbre structure Khazneh ou The Treasury, qui serait le mausolée du roi nabatéen Aretas IV, et dont la population atteindrait au maximum 20 000 habitants.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Le voyageur et poète victorien Dean Burgon a donné à Petra une description qui reste à ce jour: &quot;Rends-moi égal à l’émerveillement jalousement gardé par le soleil oriental, une ville rose aussi ancienne que le temps.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Cependant, les mots peuvent difficilement rendre justice à la magnificence de Petra. Pour mieux savourer l’atmosphère de cette merveille ancienne, visitez-le dans la tranquillité du petit matin ou en fin d’après-midi, lorsque le rocher de grès brille de rouge et de grandeur. C&#039;est certainement un must pour les visiteurs de Jordanie et du Moyen-Orient.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Petra/khazna4.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d13776.124196576167!2d35.471370226142305!3d30.321634658514736!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15016930021ab6b1:0xe43a697bc3a3e0b9!2sWadi+Musa!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564843293999!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 413, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'petra');
INSERT INTO `en33_pages` (`id`, `name`, `title`, `meta_desc`, `meta_key`, `contents`, `published`, `lang_id`, `lang`, `icon`, `layout`, `url`) VALUES
(415, 'Petra', 'Petra', 'Petra è stata dichiarata patrimonio dell&#039;umanità dall&#039;UNESCO dal 1985 e una delle nuove 7 meraviglie del mondo che incanta i visitatori provenienti da ogni angolo del globo. L&#039;UNESCO', 'Petra è stata dichiarata patrimonio dell&#039;umanità dall&#039;UNESCO dal 1985 e una delle nuove 7 meraviglie del mondo che incanta i visitatori provenienti da ogni angolo del globo. L&#039;UNESCO', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Senza dubbio il simbolo della Giordania, l&#039;attrazione più famosa e visitata è la città nabatea di Petra, incastonata nelle montagne a sud del Mar Morto. Petra, che significa &quot;pietra&quot; in greco, è forse la città antica più spettacolare che sia rimasta nel mondo moderno.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Petra è stata dichiarata patrimonio dell&#039;umanità dall&#039;UNESCO dal 1985 e una delle nuove 7 meraviglie del mondo che incanta i visitatori provenienti da ogni angolo del globo. L&#039;UNESCO l&#039;ha descritta come &quot;una delle proprietà culturali più preziose del patrimonio culturale dell&#039;uomo&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La città era la capitale dei Nabatei. Arabi che si stabilirono e dominarono nel sud della Giordania per oltre 2000 anni fa durante il periodo pre-romano. Erano particolarmente abili nel raccogliere l&#039;acqua piovana, l&#039;agricoltura e scolpivano questo paese delle meraviglie di templi, tombe ed edifici elaborati da solida roccia. Petra fiorì nel I secolo d.C., quando fu costruita la sua famosa Khazneh o la struttura del Tesoro - ritenuta il mausoleo del re nabateo Aretas IV - e la sua popolazione raggiunse il suo picco a circa 20.000 abitanti&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Il viaggiatore e poeta vittoriano Dean Burgon diede a Petra una descrizione che vale fino ai giorni nostri: &quot;Rendimi uguale alla meraviglia gelosamente custodita dal sole orientale, una città rosa antica come il tempo.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Eppure le parole difficilmente possono rendere giustizia alla magnificenza che è Petra. Per assaporare al meglio l&#039;atmosfera di questa antica meraviglia, visita nella quiete del primo mattino o nel tardo pomeriggio, quando la roccia di arenaria si illumina di rosso con calma magnificenza. È certamente una tappa obbligata per i visitatori della Giordania e del Medio Oriente.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Petra/khazna4.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d13776.124196576167!2d35.471370226142305!3d30.321634658514736!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15016930021ab6b1:0xe43a697bc3a3e0b9!2sWadi+Musa!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564843293999!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 413, 'it', '', 'one col', 'petra'),
(416, 'Wadi Rum', 'Wadi Rum', 'When you arrive in this desert it is easy to understand why it was chosen as the location of films set on the planet Mars.', 'When you arrive in this desert it is easy to understand why it was chosen as the location of films set on the planet Mars.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The Wadi Rum consists of 278 square miles of desert wilderness. It is commonly called &quot;The Valley of the Moon&quot;. This is a protected area in the southern Jordan valley.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;When you arrive to Wadi Rum it is easy to understand why it was chosen as the location of films set on the planet Mars such as the famed mainstream movie Red Planet (2000). The color of its sand and its rocks of granite, basalt and sandstone sculpted by the wind, create a natural spectacle that has few equals in the world.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;A maze of monolithic rockscapes rises up from the desert floor to heights of 1,750m creating a natural challenge for serious mountaineers. Hikers can enjoy the tranquility of the boundless empty spaces and explore the canyons and water holes to discover 4000-year-old rock drawings and the many other spectacular treasures this vast wilderness holds in store.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;For thousands of years, people have inhabited Wadi Rum, struggling to survive in this harsh desert conditions. Hunters, farmers, traders and pastoralist have called this area home. Even the famed Nabateans once resided Wadi Rum, leaving behind several structures upon their departure.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Getting on a 4x4 vehicle and entering the desert for miles will be your escape from civilization, towards a place you must find yourself, tranquility, peace and inner calm, a sense of quiet despite the incessant hiss of the wind. &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Stunning sunsets and star-filled nights, definitely make the Wadi Rum desert one of the wonders of Jordan that you have to visit.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/wadi-rum/Wadi Rum  website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d222100.77456736425!2d35.266207873795295!3d29.565157302724135!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x1500926872782d31:0x33e433bd6669a483!2sWadi+Rum+Protected+Area!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564843941559!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 416, 'en', 'fa-angle-right', 'one col', 'wadi-rum'),
(417, 'Wadi Rum', 'Wadi Rum', 'Lorsque vous arrivez à Wadi Rum, il est facile de comprendre pourquoi il a été choisi comme lieu de tournage de films tournés sur la planète Mars', 'Lorsque vous arrivez à Wadi Rum, il est facile de comprendre pourquoi il a été choisi comme lieu de tournage de films tournés sur la planète Mars', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Le Wadi Rum se compose de 278 miles carrés de désert de dessert. Il est communément appelé &quot;La Vallée de la Lune&quot;. C&#039;est une zone protégée dans la vallée du Jourdain méridionale.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Lorsque vous arrivez à Wadi Rum, il est facile de comprendre pourquoi il a été choisi comme lieu de tournage de films tournés sur la planète Mars, tels que le célèbre film grand public Red Planet (2000). La couleur de son sable et ses roches de granit, de basalte et de grès sculptés par le vent créent un spectacle naturel sans égal au monde.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Un labyrinthe de paysages rocheux monolithiques s&#039;élève depuis le sol du désert à une altitude de 1 750 m, créant un défi naturel pour les alpinistes chevronnés. Les randonneurs peuvent profiter de la tranquillité des espaces vides infinis et explorer les canyons et les points d&#039;eau pour découvrir des dessins rupestres vieux de 4000 ans et les nombreux autres trésors spectaculaires que ce vaste désert recèle.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Depuis des milliers d’années, des habitants du Wadi Rum se sont battus pour survivre dans les conditions extrêmes du désert. Les chasseurs, les agriculteurs, les commerçants et les pasteurs ont élu domicile dans cette région. Même les célèbres Nabatéens ont résidé dans le Wadi Rum, laissant derrière eux plusieurs structures à leur départ.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Monter dans un véhicule 4x4 et pénétrer dans le désert à des kilomètres sera votre évasion de la civilisation, vers un endroit où vous devez vous trouver, tranquillité, paix et calme intérieur, une sensation de calme malgré le sifflement incessant du vent.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;De superbes couchers de soleil et des nuits remplies d&#039;étoiles font du désert de Wadi Rum l&#039;une des merveilles de la Jordanie que vous devez visiter.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/wadi-rum/Wadi Rum  website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d222100.77456736425!2d35.266207873795295!3d29.565157302724135!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x1500926872782d31:0x33e433bd6669a483!2sWadi+Rum+Protected+Area!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564843941559!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 416, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'wadi-rum'),
(418, 'Wadi Rum', 'Wadi Rum', 'Quando arrivi a Wadi Rum è facile capire perché sia ​​stato scelto come location per i film ambientati sul pianeta Marte come il famoso film mainstream Red Planet', 'Quando arrivi a Wadi Rum è facile capire perché sia ​​stato scelto come location per i film ambientati sul pianeta Marte come il famoso film mainstream Red Planet', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Il Wadi Rum è costituito da 278 miglia quadrate di deserto selvaggio. È comunemente chiamato &quot;La valle della luna&quot;. Questa è un&#039;area protetta nella valle meridionale della Giordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Quando arrivi a Wadi Rum è facile capire perché sia ​​stato scelto come location per i film ambientati sul pianeta Marte come il famoso film mainstream Red Planet (2000). Il colore della sua sabbia e le sue rocce di granito, basalto e arenaria scolpite dal vento, creano uno spettacolo naturale che ha pochi eguali al mondo.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Un labirinto di paesaggi rocciosi monolitici si innalza dal pavimento del deserto ad altezze di 1.750 m creando una sfida naturale per gli alpinisti seri. Gli escursionisti possono godere della tranquillità degli sconfinati spazi vuoti ed esplorare i canyon e le pozze d&#039;acqua per scoprire disegni rocciosi di 4000 anni e molti altri tesori spettacolari che questa vasta regione selvaggia tiene in serbo.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Per migliaia di anni, le persone hanno abitato il Wadi Rum, lottando per sopravvivere in queste dure condizioni del deserto. Cacciatori, agricoltori, commercianti e pastori hanno chiamato questa zona casa. Persino i famosi Nabatei risiedevano un tempo nel Wadi Rum, lasciando diverse strutture alla loro partenza.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Salire su un veicolo 4x4 ed entrare nel deserto per chilometri sarà la tua fuga dalla civiltà, verso un luogo in cui devi trovare te stesso, la tranquillità, la pace e la calma interiore, un senso di quiete nonostante il sibilo incessante del vento.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Tramonti mozzafiato e notti piene di stelle, rendono sicuramente il deserto del Wadi Rum una delle meraviglie della Giordania che devi visitare.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/wadi-rum/Wadi Rum  website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d222100.77456736425!2d35.266207873795295!3d29.565157302724135!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x1500926872782d31:0x33e433bd6669a483!2sWadi+Rum+Protected+Area!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564843941559!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 416, 'it', '', 'one col', 'wadi-rum'),
(419, 'La Pequeña Petra', 'La Pequeña Petra', 'La pequeña Petra también se conoce en árabe como Siq al-Barid &quot;el cañón frío&quot;. Al igual que Petra, es un sitio nabateo, con edificios tallados en las paredes de los cañones de arenisca.', 'La pequeña Petra también se conoce en árabe como Siq al-Barid &quot;el cañón frío&quot;. Al igual que Petra, es un sitio nabateo, con edificios tallados en las paredes de los cañones de arenisca.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La Pequeña Petra también es conocida en árabe como Siq al-Barid &quot;el cañón frío&quot;, proviene de su orientación y sus paredes altas que impiden la entrada de la mayor parte de la luz solar disponible. Es un sitio arqueológico ubicado al Norte de Petra, en ciudad de Wadi Musa en la Gubernatura de Ma&#039;an en Jordania. Al igual que Petra, es un sitio Nabateo y, como su nombre lo indica, es mucho más pequeño que Petra; sin embargo, está repleto de tumbas, templos, triclinios o comedores, casas, canales de agua y cisternas talladas en las paredes de los cañones de arenisca.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La Pequeña Petra es parte del Parque Arqueológico de Petra, aunque se accede por separado y se incluyo en la inscripción de Petra como Patrimonio de la Humanidad por la UNESCO.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Al igual que Petra, La Pequeña Petra está abierta al público durante el día. Sin embargo, se opera por separado y no requiere un boleto de admisión y una tarifa como lo hace Petra. Los beduinos locales venden recuerdos y bocadillos en el pequeño estacionamiento. Muchos visitantes a Petra han incluido cada vez más a Pequeña Petra en sus itinerarios. Las guías lo recomiendan como menos concurrido y más relajado que el propio Petra. La Casa Pintada, que no tiene contraparte en Petra, también se ha sumado a la atracción.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;En el extremo Oeste del cañón, un conjunto de escalones conduce a la cima de la roca en este punto, un beduino ha instalado un bonito salón de té para que pueda disfrutar de la impresionante vista. También es posible caminar a través del sendero de 6 kilómetros (3.7 millas) desde el final del cañón que une Pequeña Petra al Monasterio de Petra, conocido en árabe como Ad Deir. Se aconseja a los que hacen el viaje que lo hagan con una guía, ya que el camino, aunque es obvio en muchos lugares, no está marcado formalmente. También se advierte a los excursionistas que no intenten el sendero solo, o tarde en el día, ya que las noches en la región a menudo son frías. También está prohibido ingresar a Petra sin haber pagado la admisión del sitio.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Petra/Little Petra22.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3442.1499734441923!2d35.44871971471867!3d30.37509898176327!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15016f643bc2d24b:0xafd3ecb219086144!2sTriclinium!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564842717941!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 410, 'es', '', 'one col', 'la-pequeña-petra'),
(420, 'Wadi Rum', 'Wadi Rum', 'Cuando llegas a este desierto, es fácil entender por qué fue elegido como la ubicación de las películas ambientadas en el planeta Marte.', 'Cuando llegas a este desierto, es fácil entender por qué fue elegido como la ubicación de las películas ambientadas en el planeta Marte.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El desierto Wadi Rum consta de 278 millas cuadradas de desierto salvaje. Es comúnmente llamado &quot;El Valle de la Luna&quot;. Esta es un área protegida en el sur del valle del Jordán. &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Cuando llegas a Wadi Rum, es fácil entender por qué se eligió como la ubicación de las películas ambientadas en el planeta Marte, como la famosa película principal Planeta Rojo (2000). El color de su arena y sus rocas de granito, basalto y arenisca esculpidas por el viento, crean un espectáculo natural como pocos en el Mundo.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Un laberinto de paisajes rocosos monolíticos se eleva desde el suelo del desierto hasta las alturas de 1.750 m, creando un desafío natural para los montañeros serios. Los excursionistas pueden disfrutar de la tranquilidad de los infinitos espacios vacíos y explorar los cañones y pozos de agua para descubrir dibujos rupestres de 4000 años y los muchos otros tesoros espectaculares que este vasto desierto tiene en reserva.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Durante miles de años, la gente ha habitado Wadi Rum, luchando por sobrevivir en las duras condiciones del desierto. Cazadores, granjeros, comerciantes y pastores han llamado hogar a esta área. Incluso los famosos Nabateos alguna vez residieron en Wadi Rum, dejando atrás varias estructuras a su partida.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Subirse a un vehículo 4x4 y entrar al desierto por millas será su escape de la civilización, hacia un lugar donde debe encontrarse tranquilidad, paz y calma interior, una sensación de serenidad a pesar del incesante silbido del viento.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Impresionantes puestas de sol y noches llenas de estrellas, definitivamente hacen del desierto de Wadi Rum una de las maravillas de Jordania que tienes que visitar.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/wadi-rum/Wadi Rum  website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d222100.77456736425!2d35.266207873795295!3d29.565157302724135!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x1500926872782d31:0x33e433bd6669a483!2sWadi+Rum+Protected+Area!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564843941559!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 416, 'es', '', 'one col', 'wadi-rum'),
(421, 'Petra', 'Petra', 'Sin lugar a dudas, la atracción más famosa de Jordania es la ciudad nabatea de Petra, ubicada en las montañas al sur del Mar Muerto. Petra, que significa &quot;piedra&quot; en griego..', 'Sin lugar a dudas, la atracción más famosa de Jordania es la ciudad nabatea de Petra, ubicada en las montañas al sur del Mar Muerto. Petra, que significa &quot;piedra&quot; en griego', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Sin lugar a dudas el símbolo de Jordania, la atracción más famosa y visitada es la ciudad Nabatea de Petra, ubicada en las montañas al Sur del Mar Muerto. Petra, que significa &quot;piedra&quot; en griego, es quizás la ciudad antigua más espectacular que queda en el mundo moderno.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Petra ha sido declarada Patrimonio de la Humanidad por la UNESCO desde 1985 y una de las Nuevas 7 Maravillas del Mundo que encanta a los visitantes de todos los rincones del mundo. La UNESCO lo ha descrito como &quot;una de las propiedades culturales más preciadas del patrimonio cultural del hombre&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La ciudad era la capital de los Nabateos. Árabes que se establecieron y dominaron en el Sur de Jordania durante más de 2000 años durante la época Pre-Romana. Eran particularmente hábiles para recolectar agua de lluvia, agricultura y tallaron estas maravillas tierras de templos, tumbas y edificios elaborados de roca sólida. Petra floreció en el siglo I d. C., cuando se construyó su famosa estructura Khazneh o The Treasury, que se cree que es el mausoleo del rey nabateo Aretas IV, y su población alcanzó un máximo de 20,000 habitantes.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El viajero y poeta victoriano Dean Burgon le dio a Petra una descripción que se mantiene hasta el día de hoy: &quot;Hazme igual a la maravilla celosamente guardada por el sol del Este, una ciudad rosada tan antigua como el tiempo´´.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Sin embargo, las palabras apenas pueden hacer justicia a la magnificencia que es Petra. Con el fin de saborear mejor la atmósfera de esta antigua maravilla, visite en la tranquilidad de la mañana temprano o al final de la tarde cuando la roca de arenisca brilla roja con tranquila grandeza. Sin duda es una visita obligada para los visitantes de Jordania y Oriente Medio.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Petra/khazna4.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d13776.124196576167!2d35.471370226142305!3d30.321634658514736!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15016930021ab6b1:0xe43a697bc3a3e0b9!2sWadi+Musa!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564843293999!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 413, 'es', '', 'one col', 'petra'),
(422, 'Ajloun', 'Ajloun', 'Viajando al norte de Jordania están Ajloun y definitivamente vale la pena visitar su castillo. Las colinas y los espacios verdes no tienen paralelo..', 'Viajando al norte de Jordania están Ajloun y definitivamente vale la pena visitar su castillo. Las colinas y los espacios verdes no tienen paralelo..', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Viajando al Norte de Jordania se encuentra Ajloun y su castillo, definitivamente merecen una visita. Ajlun, es la ciudad capital de la Gubernatura de Ajloun, una ciudad montañosa en el Norte de Jordania, ubicada a 76 kilómetros (alrededor de 47 millas) al noroeste de Ammán. Se destaca por sus impresionantes ruinas del castillo de Ajloun del siglo XII. Este lugar serpentea a través de fértiles colinas verdes bordeadas de olivares.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El castillo de Ajlun se encuentra en el sitio de un antiguo monasterio. Fue renovado como un fuerte en 1184 por Izz al-Din Usama, un general en el ejército de Saladino. El castillo controlaba el tráfico a lo largo de la carretera que conecta Damasco y Egipto. La fortaleza marca el límite más alejado de las incursiones francas durante las Cruzadas.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Algunas de las piedras con las que se construyó el castillo tienen cruces talladas en ellas, dando crédito a una tradición, relatada por un historiador árabe del siglo XIII que: &quot;un antiguo monasterio estuvo una vez en el sitio, habitado por un cristiano llamado Ajloun; cuando el  monasterio cayó en ruinas, el castillo tomó su lugar y el nombre del monje &quot;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Ubicada en el centro de Ajloun se encuentra la Gran Mezquita de Ajlun. Esta mezquita es una de las más antiguas que existen en Jordania y data de hace unos 800 años. Este edificio fue anteriormente una iglesia cristiana bizantina; Ha habido informes de escritura griega en las secciones más antiguas. Algunos lugareños llaman a la torre de oración &quot;el filtro&quot; (refiriéndose a un filtro de cigarrillo, porque la mitad de la torre fue construida sobre una torre cuadrada, muy probablemente un campanario de la Iglesia).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Este lugar te cautivará de seguro.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Ajlun/Ajloun website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d53934.297894855255!2d35.7322292455951!3d32.34156536287274!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151c87da460049bd:0x3fbf8443e03b269a!2sAjloun!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564839902477!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 407, 'es', '', 'one col', 'ajloun'),
(423, 'El Mar Muerto', 'El Mar Muerto', 'El Mar Muerto es uno de los paisajes naturales y espirituales más espectaculares del mundo. Este lugar único tiene un contenido extremadamente alto de sales y minerales', 'El Mar Muerto es uno de los paisajes naturales y espirituales más espectaculares del mundo. Este lugar único tiene un contenido extremadamente alto de sales y minerales', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El Mar Muerto es un lago salado bordeado por Jordania al Este e Israel y Cisjordania al Oeste. Se encuentra en el Valle del Jordán, y el río Jordán es la única fuente de agua importante que desemboca en el Mar Muerto.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Su superficie y costas están a 430.5 metros (1.412 pies) debajo del nivel del mar, la elevación más baja del Mundo en tierra. 9.6 veces más salada que el agua del océano, es uno de los cuerpos de agua más salados del mundo; debido a su salinidad, puedes flotar en el Mar Muerto sin siquiera intentarlo, lo que hace que nadar aquí sea una experiencia verdaderamente única que no debes perderte. Este lugar único tiene un contenido extremadamente alto de sales y minerales que le da a sus aguas los poderes curativos y las cualidades terapéuticas reconocidas por más de 2000 años.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Hoy en día, los visitantes de todo el mundo van al Mar Muerto para tratar diversos problemas de salud como la Psoriasis, la Climatoterapia en el Mar Muerto puede ser una terapia para la psoriasis tomando el sol durante largos períodos en el área debido a su posición bajo el nivel del mar dan como resultado que los rayos UV están parcialmente bloqueados por el aumento de la capa de nubes. Los pacientes con Rinosinusitis que recibieron irrigación nasal con solución salina del Mar Muerto mostraron un alivio mejorado de los síntomas en comparación con el aerosol de solución salina hipertónica estándar; y la Osteoartritis, la terapia de lodo del Mar Muerto se ha sugerido para aliviar temporalmente el dolor en pacientes con osteoartritis de las rodillas, el tratamiento con compresas de lodo ricas en minerales se puede utilizar para aumentar la terapia médica convencional.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El Mar Muerto es uno de los paisajes naturales y espirituales más espectaculares del mundo; hay mucho que hacer en las costas del Mar Muerto, estará encantado.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Deadsea/Dead Sea website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d435268.73507000995!2d35.21009266120768!3d31.536874322287797!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15033c2eaf9fbba1:0xf38cff48a0c15882!2sDead+Sea!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564839572942!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 404, 'es', '', 'one col', 'el-mar-muerto'),
(424, 'Monte Nebo', 'Monte Nebo', 'El Monte Nebo es uno de los sitios bíblicos que se pueden ver durante un viaje a Jordania.Según la Biblia, fue desde el Monte Nebo que Moisés contempló la Tierra Prometida..', 'El Monte Nebo es uno de los sitios bíblicos que se pueden ver durante un viaje a Jordania.Según la Biblia, fue desde el Monte Nebo que Moisés contempló la Tierra Prometida..', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El Monte Nebo es uno de los sitios bíblicos que se pueden ver durante un viaje a Jordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Según la Biblia, fue desde el Monte Nebo que Moisés contempló la Tierra Prometida después de que Dios le prohibió entrar. Además, para los cristianos, es en esta montaña donde está la tumba de Moisés. Para los musulmanes, sería en Nabi Musa, al otro lado del Jordán, en Palestina.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Como parte de las atracciones de este magnífico lugar, verá:&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;La Cruz Serpentina de Moisés (El Monumento a la Serpiente de Bronce)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Restos de la basílica de Moisés&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; Aproximadamente 1 km al este del Monte Nebo, se pueden ver los manantiales de Moisés (Ayun Musa), una colección de manantiales de agua dulce que se dice que fue Moisés durante el éxodo cuando Dios le ordenó que arrojara una rama de árbol en los manantiales amargos para que fueran lo suficientemente dulces como para beber.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Cerca del monte Nebo se encuentra el pueblo de Khirbet al-Mukkhayat. El pueblo es conocido por albergar numerosos restos bizantinos, incluidos mosaicos encontrados en la capilla del sacerdote Juan y la iglesia de los Santos.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;<br><br>&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Mount_nebo/Monte-nebo.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d13568.31599039157!2d35.71652272680265!3d31.768331250610355!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151cad7ed4c82179:0x131a1cf280726293!2sMount+Nebo!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564830031400!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 401, 'es', '', 'one col', 'monte-nebo'),
(425, 'Madaba', 'Madaba', 'Madaba es mejor conocido por sus mosaicos bizantinos y omeyas, especialmente un gran mapa de mosaicos de la Tierra Santa de la era bizantina..', 'Madaba es mejor conocido por sus mosaicos bizantinos y omeyas, especialmente un gran mapa de mosaicos de la Tierra Santa de la era bizantina..', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Madaba es la capital de la Gubernatura de Madaba, en el centro de Jordania, con una población de aproximadamente 60,000 habitantes. Es mejor conocido por sus mosaicos bizantinos y omeyas, especialmente un gran mapa de mosaicos de la Tierra Santa de la era bizantina. Madaba se encuentra a 30 kilómetros (19 millas) al suroeste de la capital, Ammán.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El pueblo de Madaba fue una vez una ciudad fronteriza moabita, mencionada en la Biblia. Madaba data de la Edad del Bronce Medio. Durante su dominio por los imperios romano y bizantino del siglo II al VII, la ciudad formó parte de la Provincia Arabia creada por el emperador romano Trajano para reemplazar el reino Nabateo de Petra.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Los principales sitios de Madaba:&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Iglesia de San Jorge, que alberga el famoso Mapa de Madaba que se descubrió en 1896 un mosaico del siglo VI que representa un mapa de Tierra Santa, a veces llamada &quot;Iglesia del Mapa&quot;. Con dos millones de piezas de piedra de colores, el mapa representa colinas, valles y pueblos. (Entrada 1 JOD, no incluida en el &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Iglesia de los Apóstoles, las ruinas de esta iglesia bizantina datan de 578 CE, y actualmente están siendo restauradas. Incluye un mosaico conocido como la &quot;Personificación del mar&quot;, que representa a una mujer que emerge del mar, rodeada de criaturas acuáticas míticas y una mezcolanza de carneros, toros, loros y vegetación exótica. El mosaico fue firmado por un mosaico llamado Salamanios. (incluido en &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Iglesia de San Giovanni Battista (Iglesia del despegue de Giovanni Battista) que ofrece una magnífica vista de la ciudad, ya que es posible subir a la cima del campanario (boleto, no incluido en el &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La ciudad es bastante agradable y además de las visitas de iglesias, es bastante agradable pasear por la ciudad y picar algo en uno de los varios restaurantes tradicionales de la ciudad.<br><br>&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Madaba/madaba mosque.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d54304.0835391128!2d35.7633807408465!3d31.71575236400819!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151cacd00bad3bc5:0x4d6d5834c1003e2b!2sMadaba!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564829017080!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 398, 'es', '', 'one col', 'madaba'),
(426, 'Los Castillos del Desierto', 'Los Castillos del Desierto', 'Extendiéndose al Este de Ammán, la llanura desértica se extiende hacia Irak y Arabia Saudita. Este es un lugar donde la arena interminable y los áridos paisajes de basalto dan prueba de la capacidad del hombre para prosperar en condiciones difíciles.', 'Extendiéndose al Este de Ammán, la llanura desértica se extiende hacia Irak y Arabia Saudita. Este es un lugar donde la arena interminable y los áridos paisajes de basalto dan prueba de la capacidad del hombre para prosperar en condiciones difíciles.', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Extendiéndose al Este de Ammán, la llanura desértica se extiende hacia Irak y Arabia Saudita. Este es un lugar donde la arena interminable y los áridos paisajes de basalto dan prueba de la capacidad del hombre para prosperar en condiciones difíciles.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El descubrimiento de hachas de mano de sílex en este desierto indica que los colonos paleolíticos habitaron la región hace aproximadamente medio millón de años. Pero los restos más notables de la habitación humana son los palacios construidos por los califas omeyas con sede en Damasco durante los primeros días del Islam (siglos VII-VIII).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Durante el apogeo de la dinastía Omeya, la arquitectura floreció con el intercambio cultural que acompañó las crecientes rutas comerciales. Para el año 750 d. C., cuando la dinastía omeya fue derrocada por los abasíes de Bagdad, una arquitectura musulmana ricamente característica estaba evolucionando, debido considerablemente a la influencia cosmopolita de los constructores y artesanos procedentes de Egipto, Mesopotamia y otros lugares de la región.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Hoy es posible ver muchas reliquias de los períodos islámicos tempranos y medievales en Jordania. Salpicado en todo el terreno estepario del Este de Jordania y las colinas centrales hay numerosas ruinas históricas, que incluyen castillos, fortalezas, torres, baños, caravanas y palacios fortificados. Conocidos colectivamente como los castillos del desierto o los palacios del desierto, originalmente formaban parte de una cadena que se extendía desde el norte de Damasco hasta Khirbet al-Mafjar, cerca de Ariha (o Jericó).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;es/qasr-al-kharanah/&quot;&gt;Qasr Al-Kharanah&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;es/qasr-amra/&quot;&gt;Qasr Amra&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Desert Castles/qasr-amra.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3202.960326365759!2d36.46056488753891!3d31.7285686252473!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b249e0321d58d:0xae2394f52625c2b!2sQasr al-Kharaneh!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569247005481!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 395, 'es', '', 'one col', 'los-castillos-del-desierto'),
(427, 'Ammán', 'La ciudad de Ammán', 'En este día podrá disfrutar de los innumerables recursos que la ciudad tiene para ofrecer, entre una caminata en el centro, una visita a sitios arqueológicos, un té caliente en Weibdeh', 'En este día podrá disfrutar de los innumerables recursos que la ciudad tiene para ofrecer, entre una caminata en el centro, una visita a sitios arqueológicos, un té caliente en Weibdeh', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Ammán es la capital y la ciudad más poblada de Jordania, y el centro económico, político y cultural del país. Situado en el centro-norte de Jordania, Ammán es el centro administrativo de la Gubernatura de Ammán. La ciudad tiene una población de 4,007,526 y una superficie de 1,680 kilómetros cuadrados (648.7 millas cuadradas). Hoy, Ammán se considera una de las ciudades árabes más modernizadas. Es un importante destino turístico en la región, particularmente entre los turistas árabes y europeos.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Ammán se divide en dos partes: la parte occidental, no solo geográficamente, llena de clubes nocturnos, pubs, comercio central y la parte oriental, que aún conserva importantes sitios arqueológicos, como la Ciudadela, el Anfiteatro Romano ... así como el &quot;suq&quot; árabe típico (mercado tradicional).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El museo más grande de Jordania es el Museo de Jordania. Contiene gran parte de los valiosos hallazgos arqueológicos en el país, incluidos algunos de los Rollos del Mar Muerto, las estatuas neolíticas de piedra caliza de &#039;Ain Ghazal y una copia de la Estela de Mesha. Otros museos incluyen la Galería Nacional de Bellas Artes de Jordania, el Museo Arqueológico de Jordania, el Museo de los Niños de Jordania, el Monumento y Museo de los Mártires, el Museo Real del Automóvil, el Museo del Profeta Mahoma, el Museo de la Vida Parlamentaria, el Museo del Folclore de Jordania y los museos en la universidad de Jordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Ammán es considerada una de las ciudades más liberales y occidentalizadas del mundo árabe. La ciudad se ha convertido en uno de los destinos más populares para expatriados occidentales y estudiantes universitarios que buscan vivir, estudiar o trabajar en el Medio Oriente. La escena culinaria de la ciudad ha cambiado desde sus puestos de shawerma y falafel para abarcar muchos restaurantes occidentales populares y locales de comida rápida como restaurantes de fusión asiática, bistros franceses y trattorias italianas.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;h5&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Amman/Royal Hotel.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d433870.8268373916!2d35.66743569022686!3d31.8354533233864!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b5fb85d7981af:0x631c30c0f8dc65e8!2sAmman!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564595824430!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 388, 'es', '', 'one col', 'amman');
