ot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt; Museo Petra &lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify; text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot;&gt;Il Museo Petra contiene 280 reperti, risalenti a epoche diverse, la mostra è composta da cinque sale che mostrano la storia di Petra...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;it/museo-petra/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Leggi di Più&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/Lowest-Point-on-Eatrh-Outside.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;The Lowest Point on Earth Museum&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt; Museo Il Posto Più Basso Della Terra&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify; text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot;&gt;Il Museo Il Posto Più Basso Della Terra, si trova a 1.329 piedi sotto il livello del mare sul bordo meridionale del...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;it/museo-il-posto-piu-basso-della-terra/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Leggi di Più&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/Amman_martyrs_memorial.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Martyrs&#039; Memorial&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt; Memoriale dei Martiri&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify; text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot;&gt;Memoriale dei Martiri è un monumento e museo ad Amman, in Giordania. Situato vicino alla città di Amman Sport...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;it/memoriale-dei-martiri/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Leggi di Più&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1013, 'it', '', 'one col', 'musei-in-giordania'),
(1018, 'Martyrs&#039; Memorial', 'Martyrs&#039; Memorial', 'Martyrs&#039; Memorial', 'Martyrs&#039; Memorial', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Martyrs&#039; Memorial is a memorial and museum in Amman, Jordan. Located next to the Amman Sport city.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The museum was established in 1977 upon King Hussein&#039;s wishes. The museum showcases a rare collection of Jordan&#039;s military weapons, clothing and vehicles.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;More than just a museum, the building is a memorial to those, The Martyrs, who gave their lives in the service of Jordan since 1915, a place where ‘the nation celebrates its victories and the state displays its history’, and honors the Hashemite dynasty in Jordan.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The museum space within the memorial comprises three interior walls or wings each hung with exhibits presenting the Great Arab Revolt, the foundation of the Emirate of Transjordan and the Arab Legion, and the development of Jordan’s armed forces.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/Amman_martyrs_memorial.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3384.055783324444!2d35.904272014669054!3d31.986503231177814!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151ca0037323ebf7:0x9b99585e56d1ea0d!2sEdifice of The Martyrs Museum!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569594063106!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1018, 'en', '', 'one col', 'martyrs-memorial'),
(1019, 'Martyrs&#039; Memorial', 'Martyrs&#039; Memorial', 'Martyrs&#039; Memorial', 'Martyrs&#039; Memorial', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Martyrs&#039; Memorial is a memorial and museum in Amman, Jordan. Located next to the Amman Sport city.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The museum was established in 1977 upon King Hussein&#039;s wishes. The museum showcases a rare collection of Jordan&#039;s military weapons, clothing and vehicles.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;More than just a museum, the building is a memorial to those, The Martyrs, who gave their lives in the service of Jordan since 1915, a place where ‘the nation celebrates its victories and the state displays its history’, and honors the Hashemite dynasty in Jordan.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The museum space within the memorial comprises three interior walls or wings each hung with exhibits presenting the Great Arab Revolt, the foundation of the Emirate of Transjordan and the Arab Legion, and the development of Jordan’s armed forces.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/Amman_martyrs_memorial.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3384.055783324444!2d35.904272014669054!3d31.986503231177814!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151ca0037323ebf7:0x9b99585e56d1ea0d!2sEdifice of The Martyrs Museum!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569594063106!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1018, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'martyrs-memorial'),
(1020, 'Monumento a los Mártires', 'Monumento a los Mártires', 'Monumento a los Mártires', 'Monumento a los Mártires', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Monumento a los Mártires es un monumento y museo en Amman, Jordania. Ubicado al lado de la ciudad de Amman Sport.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El museo fue establecido en 1977 por los deseos del rey Hussein. El museo exhibe una rara colección de armas, ropa y vehículos militares de Jordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Más que un simple museo, el edificio es un monumento conmemorativo para aquellos, los Mártires, que dieron sus vidas al servicio de Jordania desde 1915, un lugar donde &quot;la nación celebra sus victorias y el estado muestra su historia&quot;, y honra a la dinastía hachemita en Jordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El espacio del museo dentro del monumento comprende tres paredes interiores o alas, cada una con exhibiciones que presentan la Gran Revuelta Árabe, la fundación del Emirato de Transjordania y la Legión Árabe, y el desarrollo de las fuerzas armadas de Jordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/Amman_martyrs_memorial.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3384.055783324444!2d35.904272014669054!3d31.986503231177814!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151ca0037323ebf7:0x9b99585e56d1ea0d!2sEdifice of The Martyrs Museum!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569594063106!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1018, 'es', '', 'one col', 'monumento-a-los-martires'),
(1021, 'Monument des Martyrs', 'Monument des Martyrs', 'Monument des Martyrs', 'Monument des Martyrs', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Le Monument des Martyrs est un monument et un musée d&#039;Amman, en Jordanie. Situé à côté de la ville d&#039;Amman Sport.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Le musée a été créé en 1977 à la demande du roi Hussein. Le musée expose une rare collection d&#039;armes, de vêtements et de véhicules militaires jordaniens.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Plus qu&#039;un musée, le bâtiment est un mémorial pour ceux, les martyrs, qui ont donné leur vie au service de la Jordanie depuis 1915, un lieu où &quot;la nation célèbre ses victoires et où l&#039;État montre son histoire&quot; et honore la Dynastie hachémite en Jordanie.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;L&#039;espace muséal à l&#039;intérieur du monument comprend trois murs intérieurs ou ailes, chacun présentant des expositions présentant la grande révolte arabe, la fondation de l&#039;émirat de Transjordanie et la légion arabe et le développement des forces armées jordaniennes.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/Amman_martyrs_memorial.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3384.055783324444!2d35.904272014669054!3d31.986503231177814!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151ca0037323ebf7:0x9b99585e56d1ea0d!2sEdifice of The Martyrs Museum!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569594063106!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1018, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'monument-des-martyrs'),
(1022, 'Memoriale dei Martiri', 'Memoriale dei Martiri', 'Memoriale dei Martiri', 'Memoriale dei Martiri', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Memoriale dei Martiri è un monumento e museo ad Amman, in Giordania. Situato vicino alla città di Amman Sport.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Il museo è stato istituito nel 1977 per volere del re Saddam Hussein. Il museo espone una rara collezione di armi, abbigliamento e veicoli militari provenienti dalla Giordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Più che un semplice museo, l&#039;edificio è un memoriale per quelli, i martiri, che hanno dato la vita al servizio della Giordania dal 1915, un luogo in cui &quot;la nazione celebra le sue vittorie e lo stato mostra la sua storia&quot;, e onora il Dinastia hashemita in Giordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Lo spazio museale all&#039;interno del monumento comprende tre pareti o ali interne, ognuna con reperti che presentano la Grande rivolta araba, la fondazione dell&#039;Emirato di Transgiordania e della Legione araba e lo sviluppo delle forze armate giordane.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/Amman_martyrs_memorial.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3384.055783324444!2d35.904272014669054!3d31.986503231177814!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151ca0037323ebf7:0x9b99585e56d1ea0d!2sEdifice of The Martyrs Museum!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569594063106!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1018, 'it', '', 'one col', 'memoriale-dei-martiri'),
(1023, 'Best Time to Visit Jordan', 'Best Time to Visit Jordan', 'Best Time to Visit Jordan', 'Best Time to Visit Jordan', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Jordan has a hot, dry climate characterized by long, hot, dry summers and short, cool winters. Because Jordan has a great variety of microclimates and they may vary during the year, the best time for your visit depends on your expectations or needs.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The climate is influenced by Jordan&#039;s location between the subtropical aridity of the Arabian Desert areas and the subtropical humidity of the eastern Mediterranean area. January is the coldest month, with temperatures from 5°C to 10°C, and August is the hottest month at 20°C to 35°C. Daily temperatures can be very hot, especially in the summer; on some days it can be 40°C or more, especially when the Sirocco (a hot, dry southerly wind) blows.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The climate in Jordan is conditioned partly by altitude. You have the higher central and northern areas, where it can be quite cold in winter especially during December to February, but relatively cool during the summer, while the low lying areas such as the Gulf of Aqaba and the Jordan valley are hot and humid during summer, particularly during July and August, but generally pleasant in winter.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Winter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;On average, Jordan only gets 30 days of rain a year in the highlands, but rain showers tend to be sharp and short. Occasional snowfall in Amman and other mountain areas can take place during the months of January and February, but is often short and melts away pretty quickly. Even Petra can get the occasional fall, and the desert can be cold especially during the night time, but this varies from season to season and from year to year.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Aqaba on the other hand, is a nice exception, where on average, the maximum daytime temperature is around 20°C  in January, and is quite popular with Europeans visiting from northern, deep frozen countries, where it gives them the chance to escape the harsh winter, enjoy Aqaba and soak up in the sun.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;When travelling in winter to Jordan, make sure to bring plenty of warm clothes and a waterproof jacket can be of great value.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;During the peak summer months, it can get hot and is often rainless, not only in the Jordan valley and Dead Sea area, but also in the desert (including Wadi Rum), yet you need to realize that the heat in the desert is dry, so it’s a bit easier to deal with, but as in travelling to any other hot country in the summer time, a hat, protective clothes, sunscreen and staying hydrated is not to be forgotten. Summer nights tend to be a bit chilly at times, so keep a light jacket or pashmina with you.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Spring and Autumn&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;When it comes to the best months to visit Jordan, March until the end of June, and September to November are probably the most suitable. In springtime, you can even enjoy the wild flowers in bloom.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;So whether you prefer travelling during winter or summer, want to enjoy the Middle eastern sun or favors the cool breeze, head to Jordan, an all seasons destination, where each time of year guarantees you a different and great experience.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/como sacar jordan pass.jpg&quot; width=&quot;429&quot; height=&quot;400&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/weather.jpg&quot; style=&quot;text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot; width=&quot;883&quot; height=&quot;471&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.6636067987!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.26508142489433!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569845424463!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1023, 'en', '', 'one col', 'best-time-to-visit-jordan'),
(1024, 'أفضل وقت لزيارة الأردن', 'أفضل وقت لزيارة الأردن', 'Best Time to Visit Jordan', 'Best Time to Visit Jordan', '<div class=\"row\"><div class=\"md-7 align-justify d-pad-r\"><h1>أفضل وقت لزيارة الأردن</h1><p>يتمتع الأردن بمناخ حار وجاف يتميز بصيف طويل وحار وجاف وشتاء قصير وبارد. وبما أن الأردن يضم مجموعة متنوعة من المناخات المحلية، فإن أفضل وقت للزيارة يعتمد على احتياجاتك.</p><p>يعتبر شهرا مارس ويونيو، وسبتمبر ونوفمبر من أفضل الشهور لزيارة الأردن حيث يكون الطقس معتدلاً وجميلاً.</p><h2>الصيف في الأردن</h2><p>خلال أشهر الصيف القصوى، يمكن أن يصبح الطقس حاراً وجافاً، خاصة في وادي الأردن ومنطقة البحر الميت والمناطق الصحراوية مثل وادي رم.</p><h2>الشتاء في الأردن</h2><p>يكون الشتاء بارداً وقد تتساقط الثلوج أحياناً في عمان والمرتفعات الجبلية خلال شهري يناير وفبراير.</p></div><div class=\"md-5\"><img src=\"uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/weather.jpg\" class=\"full-width\" /></div></div>', 1, 1023, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'best-time-to-visit-jordan'),
(1025, 'Mejor Época Para Visitar Jordania', 'Mejor Época Para Visitar Jordania', 'Mejor Época Para Visitar Jordania', 'Mejor Época Para Visitar Jordania', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Jordania tiene un clima cálido y seco caracterizado por veranos largos, calurosos y secos e inviernos cortos y fríos. Debido a que Jordania tiene una gran variedad de microclimas y pueden variar durante el año, el mejor momento para su visita depende de sus expectativas o necesidades.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El clima está influenciado por la ubicación de Jordania entre la aridez subtropical de las áreas del desierto de Arabia y la humedad subtropical del área del Este del Mediterráneo. Enero es el mes más frío, con temperaturas de 5 ° C a 10 ° C, y Agosto es el mes más caluroso de 20 ° C a 35 ° C. Las temperaturas diarias pueden ser muy altas, especialmente en verano; en algunos días puede ser de 40 ° C o más, especialmente cuando sopla el Sirocco (un viento cálido y seco del sur).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El clima en Jordania está condicionado en parte por la altitud. Tiene las zonas más altas del centro y el Norte, donde puede hacer bastante frío en invierno, especialmente de Diciembre a Febrero, pero relativamente fresco durante el verano, mientras que las zonas bajas como el Golfo de Aqaba y el valle del Jordán son cálidos y húmedos durante el verano, particularmente durante Julio y Agosto, pero generalmente agradable en invierno.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Invierno&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;En promedio, Jordania solo recibe 30 días de lluvia al año en las tierras altas, pero las lluvias tienden a ser agudas y cortas. Las nevadas ocasionales en Amman y otras áreas montañosas pueden tener lugar durante los meses de enero y febrero, pero a menudo son cortas y se derriten rápidamente. Incluso Petra puede tener una caída ocasional, y el desierto puede ser frío, especialmente durante la noche, pero esto varía de una estación a otra y de un año a otro.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Aqaba, por otro lado, es una buena excepción, donde, en promedio, la temperatura máxima durante el día es de alrededor de 20 ° C en Enero, y es bastante popular entre los europeos que visitan países del Norte congelados, donde les da la oportunidad de escapar de la duro invierno, para disfrutar de Aqaba y tomar el sol.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Cuando viaje en invierno a Jordania, asegúrese de llevar mucha ropa abrigada y una chaqueta impermeable puede ser de gran valor.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Verano&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Durante los meses pico de verano, puede hacer calor y, a menudo, no llueve, no solo en el valle del Jordán y el área del Mar Muerto, sino también en el desierto (incluido Wadi Rum), pero debes darte cuenta de que el calor en el desierto es seco, por lo que es un poco más fácil de manejar, pero como viajar a cualquier otro país caluroso en verano, no se debe olvidar un sombrero, ropa protectora, protector solar y mantenerse hidratado. Las noches de verano tienden a ser un poco frías a veces, así que ten una chaqueta ligera o pashmina contigo.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primavera y Otoño&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Cuando se trata de los mejores meses para visitar Jordania, Marzo hasta finales de Junio y Septiembre a Noviembre son probablemente los más adecuados. En primavera, incluso puedes disfrutar de la floración de las flores silvestres.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Ya sea que prefiera viajar durante el invierno o el verano, desee disfrutar del sol del Medio Oriente o prefiera la brisa fresca, diríjase a Jordania, un destino para todas las estaciones, donde cada época del año le garantiza una experiencia diferente y excelente.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/como sacar jordan pass.jpg&quot; width=&quot;429&quot; height=&quot;400&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/weather.jpg&quot; style=&quot;text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot; width=&quot;883&quot; height=&quot;471&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.6636067987!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.26508142489433!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569845424463!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1023, 'es', '', 'one col', 'mejor-epoca-para-visitar-jordania'),
(1026, 'Meilleur Moment Pour Visiter La Jordanie', 'Meilleur Moment Pour Visiter La Jordanie', 'Meilleur Moment Pour Visiter La Jordanie', 'Meilleur Moment Pour Visiter La Jordanie', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Le meilleur moment pour votre visite dépend de vos attentes ou de vos besoins car le climat de la  Jordanie est  caractérisé par de longs étés chauds et secs et des hivers courts et froids, étant donné que cette dernière  possède une grande variété de microclimats qui peut varier au cours de l’année.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Le climat est influencé par la situation géographique de la Jordanie entre l&#039;aridité subtropicale des zones désertiques d&#039;Arabie et l&#039;humidité subtropicale de la région de la Méditerranée orientale. Janvier est le mois le plus froid, avec des températures comprises entre 5 ° C et 10 ° C, et Août est le mois le plus chaud entre 20 ° C et 35 ° C. Les températures quotidiennes peuvent être très élevées, surtout en été; certains jours, il peut atteindre 40 ° C ou plus, surtout lorsque le Sirocco souffle (vent sec et chaud du sud)&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La météo en Jordanie est en partie conditionnée par l&#039;altitude : les zones les plus hautes du centre et du nord, où il peut faire assez froid en hiver, particulièrement de décembre à février, mais relativement frais en été, tandis que les zones basses comme le golfe d&#039;Aqaba et la vallée du Jourdain sont chaudes et humide en été, particulièrement en juillet et août, mais généralement agréable en hiver.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiver&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;En moyenne, la Jordanie ne reçoit que 30 jours de pluie par an sur les hauts plateaux, mais les pluies ont tendance à être fortes et courtes. Des chutes de neige occasionnelles à Amman et dans d&#039;autres régions montagneuses peuvent avoir lieu pendant les mois de janvier et février, mais elles sont souvent courtes et fondent rapidement. Même Petra peut avoir une chute occasionnelle, et le désert peut être froid, surtout la nuit, mais cela varie d&#039;une saison à l&#039;autre et d&#039;une année à l&#039;autre.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Aqaba, en revanche, est une bonne exception. En moyenne, la température maximale au cours de la journée est de 20 ° C environ en janvier. Elle est très appréciée des Européens en visite dans les pays du Nord glacés, où elle leur donne possibilité d&#039;échapper à l&#039;hiver rigoureux, d&#039;apprécier Aqaba et de prendre un bain de soleil.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Lorsque vous voyagez en Jordanie en hiver, veillez à porter beaucoup de vêtements chauds et une veste imperméable peut être d&#039;une grande utilité.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Été&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;En été, il peut faire chaud et souvent, il ne pleut pas, non seulement dans la vallée du Jourdain,  la mer Morte, mais aussi dans le désert (y compris le Wadi Rum), mais vous devez savoir que la chaleur dans le désert est sèche, elle est donc un peu plus facile à manipuler, mais comme pour voyager dans tout autre pays chaud en été, vous ne devriez pas oublier un chapeau, des vêtements de protection, un écran solaire et rester hydraté. Les nuits d&#039;été ont tendance à être un peu froides parfois, alors ayez une veste légère ou un pashmina avec vous.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Printemps et Automne&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;En ce qui concerne les meilleurs mois pour visiter la Jordanie, mars à fin juin et septembre à novembre sont probablement les plus propices, au printemps, vous pouvez même profiter de la floraison des fleurs sauvages.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Que vous préfériez voyager en hiver ou en été, profiter du soleil du Moyen-Orient ou favoriser  la brise fraîche, dirigez-vous vers la Jordanie, une destination pour toutes les saisons, où chaque période de l&#039;année vous garantit une expérience différente et excellente.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/como sacar jordan pass.jpg&quot; width=&quot;429&quot; height=&quot;400&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/weather.jpg&quot; style=&quot;text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot; width=&quot;883&quot; height=&quot;471&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.6636067987!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.26508142489433!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569845424463!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1023, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'meilleur-moment-pour-visiter-la-jordanie');
INSERT INTO `en33_pages` (`id`, `name`, `title`, `meta_desc`, `meta_key`, `contents`, `published`, `lang_id`, `lang`, `icon`, `layout`, `url`) VALUES
(1027, 'Periodo Migliore Per Visitare La Giordania', 'Periodo Migliore Per Visitare La Giordania', 'Periodo Migliore Per Visitare La Giordania', 'Periodo Migliore Per Visitare La Giordania', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La Giordania ha un clima caldo e secco caratterizzato da estati lunghe, calde e secche e inverni brevi e freddi. Poiché la Giordania ha una grande varietà di microclimi e può variare nel corso dell&#039;anno, il momento migliore per la tua visita dipende dalle tue aspettative o necessità.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Il clima è influenzato dalla posizione della Giordania tra l&#039;aridità subtropicale delle aree desertiche arabe e l&#039;umidità subtropicale dell&#039;area del Mediterraneo orientale. Gennaio è il mese più freddo, con temperature da 5 ° C a 10 ° C, e agosto è il mese più caldo da 20 ° C a 35 ° C.Le temperature giornaliere possono essere molto elevate, soprattutto in estate; in alcuni giorni può essere di 40 ° C o più, soprattutto quando soffia lo scirocco (un caldo vento secco da sud).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Il tempo in Giordania è in parte condizionato dall&#039;altitudine. Ha le aree più alte del centro e del nord, dove può fare abbastanza freddo in inverno, soprattutto da dicembre a febbraio, ma relativamente fresco durante l&#039;estate, mentre le aree basse come il Golfo di Aqaba e la Valle del Giordano sono calde e umido durante l&#039;estate, in particolare nei mesi di luglio e agosto, ma generalmente piacevole in inverno.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inverno&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;In media, la Giordania riceve solo 30 giorni di pioggia all&#039;anno negli altopiani, ma le piogge tendono ad essere forti e brevi. Nevicate occasionali ad Amman e in altre aree montuose possono aver luogo durante i mesi di gennaio e febbraio, ma sono spesso brevi e si sciolgono rapidamente. Anche Petra può avere una caduta occasionale e il deserto può essere freddo, soprattutto di notte, ma questo varia da una stagione all&#039;altra e da un anno all&#039;altro.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Aqaba, d&#039;altra parte, è una buona eccezione, dove, in media, la temperatura massima durante il giorno è di circa 20 ° C a gennaio, ed è abbastanza popolare tra gli europei che visitano i paesi del nord congelati, dove dà loro il possibilità di fuggire dal rigido inverno, godersi Aqaba e prendere il sole.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Quando viaggi in Giordania in inverno, assicurati di indossare molti vestiti caldi e una giacca impermeabile può essere di grande valore.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Estate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Durante i mesi estivi di punta, può essere caldo e spesso non piove, non solo nella Valle del Giordano e nell&#039;area del Mar Morto, ma anche nel deserto (incluso il Wadi Rum), ma dovresti capire che il Il caldo nel deserto è secco, quindi è un po &#039;più facile da gestire, ma come viaggiare in qualsiasi altro paese caldo in estate, non dovresti dimenticare un cappello, indumenti protettivi, crema solare e rimanere idratato. Le notti estive tendono a essere un po &#039;fredde a volte, quindi porta con te una giacca leggera o una pashmina.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primavera e Autunno&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Quando si tratta dei mesi migliori per visitare la Giordania, da marzo a fine giugno e da settembre a novembre sono probabilmente i più adatti. In primavera, puoi persino goderti la fioritura dei fiori selvatici.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Se preferisci viaggiare in inverno o in estate, vuoi goderti il ​​sole del Medio Oriente o preferire la brezza fresca, vai in Giordania, una destinazione per tutte le stagioni, dove ogni momento dell&#039;anno ti garantisce un&#039;esperienza diversa ed eccellente.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/como sacar jordan pass.jpg&quot; width=&quot;429&quot; height=&quot;400&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Museum/weather.jpg&quot; style=&quot;text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot; width=&quot;883&quot; height=&quot;471&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.6636067987!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.26508142489433!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569845424463!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1023, 'it', '', 'one col', 'periodo-migliore-per-visitare-la-giordania'),
(1028, 'Queen Alia International Airport', 'Queen Alia International Airport', 'Queen Alia International Airport', 'Queen Alia International Airport', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Queen Alia International Airport is Jordan&#039;s main and largest airport and is located in Zizya 30 kilometers (20 mi) south of the capital city, Amman was established in 1983. It is named after Queen Alia who died in 1977. &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;A state-of-the-art new terminal was inaugurated in March 2013 to replace the airport&#039;s older two passenger terminals and one cargo terminal. In 2014, the new airport received the &quot;Best Improvement by Region: Middle East&quot; and &quot;Best Airport by Region: Middle East&quot; awards by the Airport Council International. The awards are given to the airports which achieved the highest customer satisfaction in the ASQ Survey.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Its main characteristic is the roof that was inspired by Bedouin tents and is composed of 127 concrete domes, each weighing up to 600 metric tons. The terminal houses several international food and beverage venues that include restaurants, supermarkets and a nuts roaster; a larger Duty Free area; children’s play area; additional shopping outlets; and internet connectivity.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/Queen_Alia_International_Airport_Terminal.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3393.7875669050773!2d35.99406441466219!3d31.72169744434789!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b5402e149d31b:0x1b38522aafb395fc!2sQueen Alia International Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569928770787!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1028, 'en', '', 'one col', 'queen-alia-international-airport'),
(1029, 'Queen Alia International Airport', 'Queen Alia International Airport', 'Queen Alia International Airport', 'Queen Alia International Airport', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Queen Alia International Airport is Jordan&#039;s main and largest airport and is located in Zizya 30 kilometers (20 mi) south of the capital city, Amman was established in 1983. It is named after Queen Alia who died in 1977. &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;A state-of-the-art new terminal was inaugurated in March 2013 to replace the airport&#039;s older two passenger terminals and one cargo terminal. In 2014, the new airport received the &quot;Best Improvement by Region: Middle East&quot; and &quot;Best Airport by Region: Middle East&quot; awards by the Airport Council International. The awards are given to the airports which achieved the highest customer satisfaction in the ASQ Survey.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Its main characteristic is the roof that was inspired by Bedouin tents and is composed of 127 concrete domes, each weighing up to 600 metric tons. The terminal houses several international food and beverage venues that include restaurants, supermarkets and a nuts roaster; a larger Duty Free area; children’s play area; additional shopping outlets; and internet connectivity.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/Queen_Alia_International_Airport_Terminal.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3393.7875669050773!2d35.99406441466219!3d31.72169744434789!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b5402e149d31b:0x1b38522aafb395fc!2sQueen Alia International Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569928770787!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1028, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'queen-alia-international-airport'),
(1030, 'Aeropuerto Internacional Queen Alia', 'Aeropuerto Internacional Queen Alia', 'Aeropuerto Internacional Queen Alia', 'Aeropuerto Internacional Queen Alia', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El Aeropuerto Internacional Queen Alia es el principal y más grande aeropuerto de Jordania y se encuentra en Zizya, a 30 kilómetros (20 millas) al Sur de la ciudad capital, Amman se estableció en 1983. Lleva el nombre de la Reina Alia, quien murió en 1977.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;En Marzo de 2013 se inauguró una nueva terminal de última generación para reemplazar las dos terminales de pasajeros y una terminal de carga más antiguas del aeropuerto. En 2014, el nuevo aeropuerto recibió los premios &quot;Mejor Mejora por Región: Medio Oriente&quot; y &quot;Mejor Aeropuerto por Región: Medio Oriente&quot; por el Consejo Internacional del Aeropuerto. Los premios se otorgan a los aeropuertos que lograron la mayor satisfacción del cliente en la Encuesta ASQ.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Su característica principal es el techo inspirado en las tiendas beduinas y está compuesto por 127 cúpulas de hormigón, cada una con un peso de hasta 600 toneladas métricas. La terminal alberga varios locales internacionales de alimentos y bebidas que incluyen restaurantes, supermercados y un tostador de nueces; un área libre de impuestos más grande; área de juegos para niños; tiendas de compras adicionales; y conectividad a internet.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/Queen_Alia_International_Airport_Terminal.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3393.7875669050773!2d35.99406441466219!3d31.72169744434789!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b5402e149d31b:0x1b38522aafb395fc!2sQueen Alia International Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569928770787!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1028, 'es', '', 'one col', 'aeropuerto-internacional-queen-alia'),
(1031, 'Aéroport International Queen Alia', 'Aéroport International Queen Alia', 'Aéroport International Queen Alia', 'Aéroport International Queen Alia', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;L&#039;Aéroport International Queen Alia est le principal et le plus grand aéroport de Jordanie. Il est situé à Zizya, à 30 km au sud de la capitale. Amman a été créé en 1983. Il porte le nom de la reine Alia, décédée en 1977.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Un nouveau terminal ultramoderne a été inauguré en mars 2013 pour remplacer les deux terminaux passagers et un ancien terminal cargo d&#039;aéroport. En 2014, le nouvel aéroport a reçu les récompenses &quot;Meilleure amélioration par région: Moyen-Orient&quot; et &quot;Meilleur aéroport par région: Moyen-Orient&quot; décernées par le Conseil international des aéroports. Les prix sont attribués aux aéroports qui ont obtenu la plus grande satisfaction de la clientèle lors du sondage ASQ.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Sa caractéristique principale est le plafond inspiré des tentes bédouines et se compose de 127 dômes en béton, pesant chacun jusqu&#039;à 600 tonnes. Le terminal abrite plusieurs magasins internationaux d’aliments et de boissons, parmi lesquels des restaurants, des supermarchés et un torréfacteur de noix; une plus grande zone hors taxe; aire de jeux pour les enfants; magasins de shopping supplémentaires; et la connectivité Internet.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/Queen_Alia_International_Airport_Terminal.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3393.7875669050773!2d35.99406441466219!3d31.72169744434789!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b5402e149d31b:0x1b38522aafb395fc!2sQueen Alia International Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569928770787!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1028, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'aeroport-international-queen-alia'),
(1032, 'Aeroporto Internazionale Queen Alia', 'Aeroporto Internazionale Queen Alia', 'Aeroporto Internazionale Queen Alia', 'Aeroporto Internazionale Queen Alia', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;L&#039;Aeroporto Internazionale Queen Alia è il principale e più grande aeroporto della Giordania e si trova a Zizya, a 30 chilometri (20 miglia) a sud della capitale, Amman è stato fondato nel 1983. Prende il nome dalla Regina Alia, che morì nel 1977.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Un nuovo terminal all&#039;avanguardia è stato inaugurato nel marzo 2013 per sostituire i due terminal passeggeri e un terminal merci aeroportuale più vecchio. Nel 2014, il nuovo aeroporto ha ricevuto il premio &quot;Miglioramento per regione: Medio Oriente&quot; e &quot;Migliore aeroporto per regione: Medio Oriente&quot; dal Consiglio internazionale degli aeroporti. I premi vengono assegnati agli aeroporti che hanno raggiunto la massima soddisfazione del cliente nel sondaggio ASQ.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La sua caratteristica principale è il soffitto ispirato alle tende beduine ed è composto da 127 cupole di cemento, ognuna delle quali pesa fino a 600 tonnellate. Il terminal ospita numerosi negozi di alimentari e bevande internazionali che includono ristoranti, supermercati e un girarrosto; una più ampia area duty-free; parco giochi per bambini; negozi supplementari; e connettività Internet.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/Queen_Alia_International_Airport_Terminal.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3393.7875669050773!2d35.99406441466219!3d31.72169744434789!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b5402e149d31b:0x1b38522aafb395fc!2sQueen Alia International Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569928770787!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1028, 'it', '', 'one col', 'aeroporto-internazionale-queen-alia'),
(1033, 'Amman Civil Airport', 'Amman Civil Airport', 'Amman Civil Airport', 'Amman Civil Airport', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Amman Civil Airport, commonly known as Marka International Airport, is located in Marka district, Greater Amman Municipality, Jordan, some 5 km north-east of Amman city center.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;It serves as Amman&#039;s a main civil airport for passengers on private flights, and moreover as an aviation education and training hub. It was the main airport for Jordan until Queen Alia International Airport was opened in 1983.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The airport was founded in 1950 by the British as a joint military civilian airport. In 2009, Jordan Airports Company officially assumed managerial and operational responsibility for Amman Civil Airport. It mainly serves now as a regional airport servicing domestic and nearby international routes, as well as charter and private VIP flights.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/ammanciviairport.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d2845.9878318961287!2d35.9817200351692!3d31.975299898664154!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b60aff165c0a5:0x8d0c19338269f08d!2sAmman Civil Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569930448882!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1033, 'en', '', 'one col', 'amman-civil-airport'),
(1034, 'Amman Civil Airport', 'Amman Civil Airport', 'Amman Civil Airport', 'Amman Civil Airport', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Amman Civil Airport, commonly known as Marka International Airport, is located in Marka district, Greater Amman Municipality, Jordan, some 5 km north-east of Amman city center.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;It serves as Amman&#039;s a main civil airport for passengers on private flights, and moreover as an aviation education and training hub. It was the main airport for Jordan until Queen Alia International Airport was opened in 1983.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The airport was founded in 1950 by the British as a joint military civilian airport. In 2009, Jordan Airports Company officially assumed managerial and operational responsibility for Amman Civil Airport. It mainly serves now as a regional airport servicing domestic and nearby international routes, as well as charter and private VIP flights.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/ammanciviairport.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d2845.9878318961287!2d35.9817200351692!3d31.975299898664154!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b60aff165c0a5:0x8d0c19338269f08d!2sAmman Civil Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569930448882!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1033, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'amman-civil-airport'),
(1035, 'Aeropuerto Civil de Ammán', 'Aeropuerto Civil de Ammán', 'Aeropuerto Civil de Ammán', 'Aeropuerto Civil de Ammán', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El Aeropuerto Civil de Ammán, comúnmente conocido como Aeropuerto Internacional de Marka, está ubicado en el distrito de Marka, Municipio de Gran Ammán, Jordania, a unos 5 km al Noreste del centro de la ciudad de Ammán.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Sirve como el principal aeropuerto civil de Amman para pasajeros en vuelos privados, y además como un centro de educación y entrenamiento de aviación. Fue el principal aeropuerto de Jordania hasta que el Aeropuerto Internacional Reina Alia se abrió en 1983.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El aeropuerto fue fundado en 1950 por los británicos como un aeropuerto civil militar conjunto. En 2009, Jordan Airports Company asumió oficialmente la responsabilidad administrativa y operativa del Aeropuerto Civil de Amman. Ahora sirve principalmente como un aeropuerto regional que da servicio a rutas nacionales e internacionales cercanas, así como vuelos charter y VIP privados.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/ammanciviairport.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d2845.9878318961287!2d35.9817200351692!3d31.975299898664154!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b60aff165c0a5:0x8d0c19338269f08d!2sAmman Civil Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569930448882!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1033, 'es', '', 'one col', 'aeropuerto-civil-de-amman'),
(1036, 'Aéroport Civil d’Amman', 'Aéroport Civil d’Amman', 'Aéroport Civil d’Amman', 'Aéroport Civil d’Amman', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;L’Aéroport Civil d’Amman, communément appelé Aéroport International de Marka, est situé dans le district de Marka, dans la municipalité du Grand Amman, en Jordanie, à environ 5 km au nord-est du centre-ville d’Amman.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Il s&#039;agit du principal aéroport civil d&#039;Amman pour les passagers des vols privés, ainsi que d&#039;un centre de formation et d&#039;éducation à l&#039;aviation. C&#039;était l&#039;aéroport principal en Jordanie jusqu&#039;à l&#039;ouverture de l&#039;aéroport international Reina Alia en 1983.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;L’aéroport a été fondé en 1950 par les Britanniques en tant qu’aéroport civil et civil mixte. En 2009, Jordan Airports Company a officiellement assumé la responsabilité administrative et opérationnelle de l&#039;aéroport civil d&#039;Amman. Il sert maintenant principalement d’aéroport régional desservant des liaisons nationales et internationales à proximité, ainsi que des vols charters privés et VIP.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/ammanciviairport.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d2845.9878318961287!2d35.9817200351692!3d31.975299898664154!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b60aff165c0a5:0x8d0c19338269f08d!2sAmman Civil Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569930448882!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1033, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'aeroport-civil-d-amman'),
(1037, 'Aeroporto Civile di Amman', 'Aeroporto Civile di Amman', 'Aeroporto Civile di Amman', 'Aeroporto Civile di Amman', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;L&#039;Aeroporto Civile di Amman, comunemente noto come Aeroporto Internazionale Marka, si trova nel distretto di Marka, nel comune di Greater Amman, in Giordania, a circa 5 km a nord-est del centro di Amman.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Serve come principale aeroporto civile di Amman per i passeggeri su voli privati e anche come centro di istruzione e formazione aeronautica. È stato il principale aeroporto della Giordania fino all&#039;apertura dell&#039;aeroporto internazionale Reina Alia nel 1983.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;L&#039;aeroporto è stato fondato nel 1950 dagli inglesi come aeroporto civile militare congiunto. Nel 2009, Jordan Airports Company ha assunto la responsabilità amministrativa e operativa dell&#039;aeroporto civile di Amman. Ora serve principalmente come aeroporto regionale che serve rotte nazionali e internazionali vicine, nonché voli charter e VIP privati.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/ammanciviairport.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d2845.9878318961287!2d35.9817200351692!3d31.975299898664154!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b60aff165c0a5:0x8d0c19338269f08d!2sAmman Civil Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569930448882!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1033, 'it', '', 'one col', 'aeroporto-civile-di-amman'),
(1038, 'King Hussein International Airport', 'King Hussein International Airport', 'King Hussein International Airport', 'King Hussein International Airport', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Aqaba Airport also known as King Hussein International Airport is an airport located in the vicinity of Industrial City, northern suburb of Aqaba in Jordan.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Annual Capacity 1,000,000, the airport has 4 check-in desks, 2 gates, a cargo building and a cargo apron together with a parallel taxiway. The airport has one baggage claim belt, 200 short term parking spaces, a Post Office, Bank, Cafeterias, VIP Lounge, Duty Free Shop, and Gift Shops, and a clinic.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The airport includes also buildings for the Ayla Aviation Academy, the Royal Jordanian Academy, the Aero Wings for Industry&#039;s assembly plant for light planes, the Jordan Private Jets Services (JPJets)&#039;s private jet terminal, and the Al Baddad International Group&#039;s maintenance centre.  A new cargo terminal (6000 m2) and a new cargo apron (220x600 m) opened in January 2005.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/Aqaba-Airport.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d8015.128124004896!2d35.01870437515073!3d29.61260183983607!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f47adc6e083:0x436bd9e1e7d5f9e6!2sKing Hussein International Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569931381261!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1038, 'en', '', 'one col', 'king-hussein-international-airport'),
(1039, 'King Hussein International Airport', 'King Hussein International Airport', 'King Hussein International Airport', 'King Hussein International Airport', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Aqaba Airport also known as King Hussein International Airport is an airport located in the vicinity of Industrial City, northern suburb of Aqaba in Jordan.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Annual Capacity 1,000,000, the airport has 4 check-in desks, 2 gates, a cargo building and a cargo apron together with a parallel taxiway. The airport has one baggage claim belt, 200 short term parking spaces, a Post Office, Bank, Cafeterias, VIP Lounge, Duty Free Shop, and Gift Shops, and a clinic.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The airport includes also buildings for the Ayla Aviation Academy, the Royal Jordanian Academy, the Aero Wings for Industry&#039;s assembly plant for light planes, the Jordan Private Jets Services (JPJets)&#039;s private jet terminal, and the Al Baddad International Group&#039;s maintenance centre.  A new cargo terminal (6000 m2) and a new cargo apron (220x600 m) opened in January 2005.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/Aqaba-Airport.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d8015.128124004896!2d35.01870437515073!3d29.61260183983607!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f47adc6e083:0x436bd9e1e7d5f9e6!2sKing Hussein International Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569931381261!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1038, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'king-hussein-international-airport'),
(1040, 'Aeropuerto Internacional King Hussein', 'Aeropuerto Internacional King Hussein', 'Aeropuerto Internacional King Hussein', 'Aeropuerto Internacional King Hussein', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El Aeropuerto de Aqaba, también conocido como Aeropuerto Internacional King Hussein, es un aeropuerto ubicado en las cercanías de Industrial City, un suburbio al Norte de Aqaba en Jordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Capacidad anual 1,000,000, el aeropuerto cuenta con 4 mostradores de facturación, 2 puertas, un edificio de carga y una plataforma de carga junto con una calle de rodaje paralela. El aeropuerto tiene un cinturón de reclamo de equipaje, 200 espacios de estacionamiento a corto plazo, una oficina de correos, banco, cafeterías, sala VIP, tienda libre de impuestos y tiendas de regalos, y una clínica.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El aeropuerto también incluye edificios para la Academia de Aviación de Ayla, la Academia Real de Jordania, la planta de ensamblaje de Aero Wings for Industry para aviones ligeros, la terminal de jets privados de Jordan Private Jets Services (JPJets) y el centro de mantenimiento de Al Baddad International Group. En enero de 2005 se inauguró una nueva terminal de carga y una nueva plataforma de carga.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/Aqaba-Airport.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d8015.128124004896!2d35.01870437515073!3d29.61260183983607!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f47adc6e083:0x436bd9e1e7d5f9e6!2sKing Hussein International Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569931381261!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1038, 'es', '', 'one col', 'aeropuerto-internacional-king-hussein'),
(1041, 'Aéroport International King Hussein', 'Aéroport International King Hussein', 'Aéroport International King Hussein', 'Aéroport International King Hussein', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;L&#039;Aéroport d&#039;Aqaba, également appelé Aéroport International King Hussein, est un aéroport situé à proximité de Industrial City, une banlieue située au nord d&#039;Aqaba, en Jordanie.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Avec une capacité annuelle de 1 000 000, l’aéroport dispose de 4 comptoirs d’enregistrement, de 2 portes, d’un bâtiment cargo, d’un quai de chargement et d’une voie de circulation parallèle. L&#039;aéroport dispose d&#039;une ceinture de récupération des bagages, de 200 places de stationnement de courte durée, d&#039;un bureau de poste, d&#039;une banque, de cafés, d&#039;un salon VIP, d&#039;une boutique hors taxes, de boutiques de souvenirs et d&#039;une clinique.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;L&#039;aéroport comprend également des bâtiments pour l&#039;Académie de l&#039;aviation d&#039;Ayla, la Royal Jordan Academy, l&#039;usine d&#039;assemblage d&#039;avions légers Aero Wings for Industry, le terminal de jets privés Jordan Services Jets (JPJets) et le centre de maintenance. du groupe international Al Baddad. Un nouveau terminal cargo et une nouvelle plate-forme cargo ont été inaugurés en janvier 2005.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/Aqaba-Airport.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d8015.128124004896!2d35.01870437515073!3d29.61260183983607!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f47adc6e083:0x436bd9e1e7d5f9e6!2sKing Hussein International Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569931381261!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1038, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'aeroport-international-king-hussein'),
(1042, 'Aeroporto Internazionale King Hussein', 'Aeroporto Internazionale King Hussein', 'Aeroporto Internazionale King Hussein', 'Aeroporto Internazionale King Hussein', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;L&#039;Aeroporto di Aqaba, noto anche come Aeroporto Internazionale King Hussein, è un aeroporto situato vicino alla città industriale, un sobborgo a nord di Aqaba in Giordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;1.000.000 di capacità annuale, l&#039;aeroporto dispone di 4 banchi check-in, 2 porte, un edificio merci e una piattaforma di carico insieme a una pista di rullaggio parallela. L&#039;aeroporto ha una cintura di ritiro bagagli, 200 parcheggi per soste brevi, un ufficio postale, banca, caffetterie, sala VIP, negozi duty-free e negozi di articoli da regalo e una clinica.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;L&#039;aeroporto comprende anche edifici per l&#039;Ayla Academy of Aviation, la Royal Jordan Academy, l&#039;impianto di assemblaggio di aeromobili leggeri Aero Wings for Industry, il terminal dei jet privati ​​Jordan Private Jets Services (JPJets) e il centro di manutenzione dal gruppo internazionale Al Baddad. Nel gennaio 2005 sono stati inaugurati un nuovo terminal merci e una nuova piattaforma cargo.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/Aqaba-Airport.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d8015.128124004896!2d35.01870437515073!3d29.61260183983607!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f47adc6e083:0x436bd9e1e7d5f9e6!2sKing Hussein International Airport!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569931381261!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1038, 'it', '', 'one col', 'aeroporto-internazionale-king-hussein'),
(1043, 'Airports in Jordan', 'Airports in Jordan', 'Airports in Jordan', 'Airports in Jordan', '&lt;div class=&quot;row &quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/Queen_Alia_International_Airport_Terminal.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Queen Alia International Airport&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt; Queen Alia International Airport&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify; text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot;&gt;Queen Alia International Airport is Jordan&#039;s main and largest airport and is located in Zizya 30 kilometers (20 mi) south of the capital city...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;en/queen-alia-international-airport/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Read More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/ammanciviairport.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Amman Civil Airport&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt; Amman Civil Airport&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify; text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot;&gt;Amman Civil Airport, commonly known as Marka International Airport, is located in Marka district, Greater Amman Municipalit...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;en/amman-civil-airport/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Read More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan Airport/Aqaba-Airport.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;King Hussein International Aiport&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text &quot;&gt; King Hussein International Airport&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Aqaba Airport also known as King Hussein International Airport is an airport located in the vicinity of Industrial City, northern suburb of Aqaba&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify; text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot;&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;en/king-hussein-international-airport/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;Read More&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1043, 'en', '', 'one col', 'airports-in-jordan'),
(1044, 'مطارات الأردن', 'مطارات الأردن', 'Airports in Jordan', 'Airports in Jordan', '&lt;div class=&quot;row &quot;&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-4 d-pad&quot;&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/airports/queen-alia-airport.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;مطار الملكة علياء الدولي&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; /&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text&quot;&gt;مطار الملكة علياء الدولي&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;مطار الملكة علياء الدولي هو المطار الرئيسي في الأردن ويقع على بُعد 35 كم جنوب عمان.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;Ar/queen-alia-international-airport/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;المزيد&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-4 d-pad&quot;&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/airports/amman-civil-airport.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;مطار عمان المدني&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; /&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text&quot;&gt;مطار عمان المدني (ماركا)&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;يقع مطار عمان المدني في شرق عمان ويخدم الرحلات الداخلية والإقليمية.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;Ar/amman-civil-airport/&quot; class=&quot;btn orange h-pad&quot;&gt;المزيد&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-4 d-pad&quot;&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/airports/king-hussein-airport.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;مطار الملك حسين الدولي&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; /&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;orange-text&quot;&gt;مطار الملك حسين الدولي&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;يقع في مدينة العقبة جنوب الأردن ويخدم السياح القادمين لزيارة البحر الأحمر والبتراء.&