a-truncate=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Sales department for Italian &amp;amp; Spanish in PV Travels Groups&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot; data-truncate=&quot;2&quot;&gt; &lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;pad-t align-right&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;&lt;em class=&quot;ic-facebook-rect &quot;&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;#&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;&lt;em class=&quot;ic-linkedin-rect &quot;&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;#&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;&lt;em class=&quot;ic-twitter &quot;&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 366, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'our-team');
INSERT INTO `en33_pages` (`id`, `name`, `title`, `meta_desc`, `meta_key`, `contents`, `published`, `lang_id`, `lang`, `icon`, `layout`, `url`) VALUES
(1393, 'Dana Biosphere Reserve', 'Dana Biosphere Reserve', 'Dana Biosphere Reserve', 'Dana Biosphere Reserve', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Dana Biosphere Reserve is Jordan&#039;s largest nature reserve, located in south-central Jordan. Dana Biosphere Reserve was founded in 1989 in the area in and around the Dana village and Wadi Dana comprising 308 square kilometres (119 sq mi).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The people of the Ata&#039;ta (or Al Atata) tribe are the native inhabitants of Dana Biosphere Reserve. Their history in Dana dates 400 years, but their original settlement in the area dates more than 6000 years. Besides the presence of the Ata&#039;ta people, archeological discoveries suggest Palaeolithic, Egyptian, Nabataean, and Roman settlement in Dana.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Dana Biosphere Reserve drops from an altitude of 1,500 metres (4,900 ft) on the Qadisiyah plateau to the low-lying desert area of Wadi Araba. The varied geology of Dana contains limestone, sandstone, and granite. The area of Wadi Dana features wind-cut sandstone cliffs. Dana is the only nature reserve in Jordan that crosses four bio-geographical zones; Mediterranean, Irano-Turanian, Saharo-Arabian, and Sudanian penetration.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The diverse environment of Dana is home to 703 plant species, 215 species of birds, and 38 species of mammals. Dana is the most diverse area of plant life in the country, consisting of numerous vegetation types including: Phoenician juniper, evergreen oak, sand dunes, acacia, and rocky sudanian. Dana is the southernmost area in the world to host the Mediterranean cypress, Cupressus sempervirens. Of the hundreds of plants species inhabiting Dana, three can be found nowhere else in the world. Many plants, especially trees and shrubs, grow in the highlands of the nature reserve.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The Nubian ibex, Syrian serin, caracal, and lesser kestrel are natives of Wadi Dana.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Dana/DanaReserve.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d130545.41267706566!2d35.41421210493362!3d30.70507101520399!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x1503c4aa62495d51:0x5272a01aefeb1b7b!2sDana Biosphere Reserve!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1567434620456!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 445, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'dana-biosphere-reserve'),
(1394, 'Wadi Rum', 'Wadi Rum', 'Wadi Rum', 'Wadi Rum', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The Wadi Rum consists of 278 square miles of dessert wilderness. It is commonly called ´´The Valley of the Moon´´. This is a protected area in the southern Jordan valley.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;When you arrive to Wadi Rum it is easy to understand why it was chosen as the location of films set on the planet Mars such as the famed mainstream movie Red Planet (2000). The color of its sand and its rocks of granite, basalt and sandstone sculpted by the wind, create a natural spectacle that has few equals in the world.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;A maze of monolithic rockscapes rises up from the desert floor to heights of 1,750m creating a natural challenge for serious mountaineers. Hikers can enjoy the tranquility of the boundless empty spaces and explore the canyons and water holes to discover 4000-year-old rock drawings and the many other spectacular treasures this vast wilderness holds in store.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;For thousands of years, people have inhabited Wadi Rum, struggling to survive in this harsh desert conditions. Hunters, farmers, traders and pastoralist have called this area home. Even the famed Nabateans once resided Wadi Rum, leaving behind several structures upon their departure.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Getting on a 4x4 vehicle and entering the desert for miles will be your escape from civilization, towards a place you must find yourself, tranquility, peace and inner calm, a sense of quiet despite the incessant hiss of the wind. &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Stunning sunsets and star-filled nights, definitely make the Wadi Rum desert one of the wonders of Jordan that you have to visit.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/wadi-rum/Wadi Rum  website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d222100.77456736425!2d35.266207873795295!3d29.565157302724135!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x1500926872782d31:0x33e433bd6669a483!2sWadi+Rum+Protected+Area!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564843941559!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 416, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'wadi-rum'),
(1395, 'Azraq', 'Azraq', 'Azraq', 'Azraq', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Azraq means &quot;The Blue&quot; in Arabic, it is a small town in Zarqa Governorate in central-eastern Jordan, 100 kilometres (62 mi) east of Amman. Azraq has long been an important settlement in a remote and now-arid desert area of Jordan. The strategic value of the town and its castle (Qasr Azraq) is that it lies in the middle of the Azraq oasis, the only permanent source of fresh water in approximately 12,000 square kilometres of desert.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The town is located on a major desert route that would have facilitated trade within the region. The Azraq oasis has a long history beginning in the Lower Palaeolithic period. Many Palaeolithic sites have been documented in the Azraq Wetlands Reserve. During the Epipalaeolithic period the oasis was also an important focus of settlement.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Nabatean period settlement activity has also been documented in the area. Qasr Azraq was built by the Romans in the 3rd century AD, and was heavily modified in the Middle Ages by the Mameluks. In the Umayyad period a water reservoir was constructed in southern Azraq. During the Arab Revolt in the early 20th century, Qasr Azraq was an important headquarters for T. E. Lawrence.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The separate and larger Shaumari reserve is also close to Azraq, being only 10 kilometres (6.2 mi) south of the town. The Shaumari Wild Reserve is a breeding centre for some of the most endangered and rare wildlife in the Middle East. In this small reserve there is a large herd of magnificent Arabian Oryx. There are also ostriches, onagers and graceful desert gazelles. These animals are protected from the hunting and habitat destruction that once threatened their existence. The Shawmari Reserve supports a rich variety of desert plants, including Atriplex, a natural food source for the Onager and Oryx.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Azraq/Azraq.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d11401.630850688458!2d36.815294921211134!3d31.83247760249731!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151aefcf61ef9c43:0x51bd54d22be06412!2sAzraq!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1567432850018!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 441, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'azraq'),
(1396, 'Aqaba', 'Aqaba', 'Aqaba', 'Aqaba', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Aqaba is the only coastal city in Jordan and the largest and most populous city on the Gulf of Aqaba. Situated in southernmost Jordan, Aqaba is the administrative centre of the Aqaba Governorate. Today, Aqaba plays a major role in the development of the Jordanian economy, through the vibrant trade and tourism sectors. The Port of Aqaba also serves other countries in the region.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Aqaba&#039;s strategic location at the northeastern tip of the Red Sea between the continents of Asia and Africa, has made its port important over the course of thousands of years&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Aqaba&#039;s location next to Wadi Rum and Petra has placed it in Jordan&#039;s golden triangle of tourism, which strengthened the city&#039;s location on the world map and made it one of the major tourist attractions in Jordan.The city is administered by the Aqaba Special Economic Zone Authority, which has turned Aqaba into a low-tax, duty-free city, attracting several mega projects like Ayla Oasis, Saraya Aqaba, Marsa Zayed and expansion of the Port of Aqaba. They are expected to turn the city into a major tourism hub in the region. However, industrial and commercial activities remain important, due to the strategic location of the city as the country&#039;s only seaport.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Excavations at Tall Hujayrat Al-Ghuzlan and Tall Al-Magass in Aqaba revealed that the city has been an inhabited settlement since 4000 BC, with a thriving copper production on a large scale. This period is largely unknown due to the absence of written historical sources. Archaeologists from University of Jordan have discovered the sites, where they found a small building whose walls were inscribed with human and animal drawings, suggesting that the building was used as a religious site.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The people who inhabited the site had developed an extensive water system in irrigating their crops which was mostly grapes and wheat. Several different-sized clay pots were also found suggesting that copper production was a major industry in the region, the pots were used in melting the copper and reshaping it. Scientific studies performed on site revealed that it had undergone two earthquakes, with the latter one leaving the site completely destroyed.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Aqaba/Aqaba website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d222065.98469071987!2d34.93504817367495!3d29.580974377533497!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15007039ff2efa81:0x595faa556d2e6acc!2sAqaba!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1567429408155!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 437, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'aqaba'),
(1397, 'Tomb of Aaron', 'Tomb of Aaron', 'Tomb of Aaron', 'Tomb of Aaron', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The Tomb of Aaron is the name of the supposed burial place of Aaron, the brother of Moses. There are two descriptions of its location in the Pentateuch, and different interpretations of its location. Although in Jewish tradition, the location of Aaron’s grave, like that of Moses, is shrouded in mystery, the Islamic tradition places it on Mount Hor, near Petra in Jordan.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Mount Hor is usually associated with the mountain near Petra in Jordan, known in Arabic as Jabal Hārūn (Aaron&#039;s Mountain) which is the highest peak in the area at 1350 meters above sea level, upon the summit of which a white-domed mosque was built in the 14th century, commemorates this. Indeed, Josephus and Eusebius both describe its location above the city of Petra.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;It has long been a place of pilgrimage for many people around the World, and is worth a trip if you have an extra day in Petra. Good physical fitness is required for the long hike there and back.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Petra/df82e914176ce65aacd067c64bd46e1c.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d58385.40267440271!2d35.40021674186123!3d30.314549972328816!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15016e0979667d99:0x1e772ea247cdc050!2sTomb of Prophet Aaron!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1567438509722!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 433, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'tomb-of-aaron'),
(1398, 'Petra', 'Petra', 'Petra', 'Petra', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Undoubtedly the symbol of Jordan, the most famous and visited attraction is the Nabatean city of Petra, nestled away in the mountains south of the Dead Sea. Petra, means &quot;stone&quot; in Greek, is perhaps the most spectacular ancient city remaining in the modern world.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Petra has been a UNESCO World Heritage site since 1985 and one of the New 7 Wonders of the World that enchants visitors from all corners of the Globe. UNESCO has described it as &quot;one of the most precious cultural properties of man&#039;s cultural heritage&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The city was the capital of the Nabataeans. Arabs who settled and dominated in southern Jordan for more than 2000 years ago during pre-Roman times. They were particularly skillful in harvesting rainwater, agriculture and carved this wonderland of temples, tombs and elaborate buildings out of solid rock. Petra flourished in the 1st century AD, when its famous Khazneh or The Treasury structure – believed to be the mausoleum of Nabataean king Aretas IV – was constructed, and its population peaked at an estimated 20,000 inhabitants&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The victorian traveler and poet Dean Burgon gave Petra a description which holds to this day -&quot;Match me such a marvel save in Eastern clime, a rose-red city half as old as time.&quot;  &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Yet words can hardly do justice to the magnificence that is Petra. In order to best savor the atmosphere of this ancient wonder, visit in the quiet of the early morning or late afternoon when the sandstone rock glows red with quiet grandeur. It is certainly a must-see for visitors to Jordan and the Middle East.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Petra/khazna4.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d13776.124196576167!2d35.471370226142305!3d30.321634658514736!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15016930021ab6b1:0xe43a697bc3a3e0b9!2sWadi+Musa!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564843293999!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 413, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'petra'),
(1399, 'Little Petra', 'Little Petra', 'Little Petra', 'Little Petra', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Little Petra is also known in Arabic as Siq al-Barid &quot;the cold canyon&quot;, comes from its orientation and its high walls preventing the entry of most available sunlight. It is an archaeological site located north of Petra and the town of Wadi Musa in the Ma&#039;an Governorate of Jordan. Like Petra, it is a Nabataean site and as its name suggests it is much smaller than Petra; however, is crammed with tombs, temples, triclinium or dining room, houses, water channels and cisterns carved into the walls of the sandstone canyons.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Little Petra is part of the Petra Archeological Park, though accessed separately, and included in Petra&#039;s inscription as a UNESCO World Heritage Site.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Like Petra, Little Petra is open to the public during the daytime. It is, however, operated separately, and does not require an admission ticket and fee as Petra does. The local Bedouins sell souvenirs and snacks in the small parking lot. Many visitors to Petra have increasingly been including Little Petra on their itineraries. Guidebooks recommend it as less crowded and more relaxed than Petra itself. The Painted House, which has no counterpart at Petra, has also added to the attraction.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;At the west end of the canyon a set of steps leads to the top of the rock at this point a Bedouin has installed a nice tearoom so you can enjoy the stunning view. It is also possible to hike via the 6-kilometre (3.7 mi) trail from the end of the canyon that unites Little Petra to Petra´s Monastery known in Arabic as Ad Deir. Those who make the journey are advised to do so with a guide as the trail, while obvious in many places, is not formally marked. Hikers are also cautioned against attempting the trail alone, or late in the day, as nights in the region are often cold. It is also forbidden to enter Petra without having paid the site&#039;s admission.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Petra/Little Petra 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3442.1499734441923!2d35.44871971471867!3d30.37509898176327!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15016f643bc2d24b:0xafd3ecb219086144!2sTriclinium!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564842717941!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 410, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'little-petra'),
(1400, 'Ajloun', 'Ajloun', 'Ajloun', 'Ajloun', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Travelling north of Jordan, Ajloun and its Castle definitely worth a visit. Ajlun, is the capital town of the Ajloun Governorate, a hilly town in the north of Jordan, located 76 kilometers (around 47 miles) north west of Amman. It is noted for its impressive ruins of the 12th-century Ajloun Castle. This place winds through fertile green hills lined with olive groves.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Ajlun Castle is located on the site of an old monastery. It was renovated as a fort in 1184 by Izz al-Din Usama, a general in the army of Saladin. The castle controlled traffic along the road connecting Damascus and Egypt. The fortress marks the furthest limit of Frankish incursions during the Crusades.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Some of the stones with which the castle was built have crosses carved into them, giving credence to a tradition, recounted by a 13th century Arab historian that: &quot;an ancient monastery once stood on the site, inhabited by a Christian named Ajloun; when the monastery fell into ruin, the castle took its place and the name of the monk&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Located in the center of Ajloun is the Great Ajlun Mosque. This mosque is one of the oldest extant in Jordan and dates back around 800 years. This edifice was previously a Byzantine Christian church; there have been reports of Greek writing in the oldest sections. The prayer tower is called &quot;the filter&quot; by some locals (referring to a cigarette filter, because half of the tower was built over a square tower, most likely a Church bell tower).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;This place will captivate you for sure.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Ajlun/Ajloun website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d53934.297894855255!2d35.7322292455951!3d32.34156536287274!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151c87da460049bd:0x3fbf8443e03b269a!2sAjloun!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564839902477!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 407, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'ajloun'),
(1401, 'Dead Sea', 'Dead Sea', 'Dead Sea', 'Dead Sea', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The Dead Sea is a salt lake bordered by Jordan to the East and Israel and the West Bank to the West. It lies in the Jordan Rift Valley, and the Jordan River is the only major water source flowing into the Dead Sea.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Its surface and shores are 430.5 meters (1,412 ft) below sea level, Earth&#039;s lowest elevation on land. 9.6 times as salty as the ocean water, it is one of the world&#039;s saltiest bodies of water; because its salinity you can float in the Dead Sea without even trying, which makes swimming here a truly unique experience not to be missed. This unique place has extremely high content of salts and minerals which gives its waters the curative powers and therapeutic qualities recognized for more than 2000 years ago.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Nowadays visitors from all over the World go to the Dead Sea to treat various health problems such as Psoriasis, the Climatotherapy at the Dead Sea may be a therapy for psoriasis by sunbathing for long periods in the area due to its position below sea level and subsequent result that UV rays are partially blocked by the increased cloud cover. Rhinosinusitis patients receiving Dead Sea saline nasal irrigation exhibited improved symptom relief compared to standard hypertonic saline spray and Osteoarthritis, Dead Sea mud pack therapy has been suggested to temporarily relieve pain in patients with osteoarthritis of the knees,  treatment with mineral-rich mud compresses can be used to augment conventional medical therapy.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The Dead Sea is one of the most spectacular natural and spiritual landscapes in the whole World; there is much to do on the shores of the Dead Sea, you will be delighted.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Deadsea/Dead Sea website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d435268.73507000995!2d35.21009266120768!3d31.536874322287797!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15033c2eaf9fbba1:0xf38cff48a0c15882!2sDead+Sea!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564839572942!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 404, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'the-dead-sea'),
(1402, 'Mount Nebo', 'Mount Nebo', 'Mount Nebo', 'Mount Nebo', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Mount Nebo is one of the biblical sites that can be seen during your trip to Jordan.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;According to the Bible, it was from Mount Nebo that Moses contemplated the Promised Land after God forbade him to enter. Moreover, for Christians, it is on this mountain where the tomb of Moses is. For Muslims, it would be in Nabi Musa, on the other side of the Jordan, in Palestine.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;As part of the attractions of this magnificent place you will see:&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;The Serpentine Cross of Moses (The Brazen Serpent Monument)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Remains of the Basilica of Moses &lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;About 1 km East of Mount Nebo, you can see the springs of Moses (Ayun Musa), are a collection of fresh water springs said to be where Moses during the Exodus was directed by God to throw a tree branch, possibly a barberry into the bitter springs to make them sweet enough to drink.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Near Mount Nebo is the village of Khirbet al-Mukkhayat. The village is known for hosting numerous Byzantine remains including mosaics found in the chapel of the priest John and the church of Saints.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;<br><br>&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Mount_nebo/Monte-nebo.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d13568.31599039157!2d35.71652272680265!3d31.768331250610355!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151cad7ed4c82179:0x131a1cf280726293!2sMount+Nebo!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564830031400!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 401, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'mount-nebo'),
(1403, 'Madaba', 'Madaba', 'Madaba', 'Madaba', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Madaba is the capital city of Madaba Governorate in central Jordan, with a population of about 60,000. It is best known for its Byzantine and Umayyad mosaics, especially a large Byzantine-Era mosaic map of the Holy Land. Madaba is located 30 kilometres (19 miles) south-west of the capital Amman.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The town of Madaba was once a Moabite border city, mentioned in the Bible. Madaba dates from the Middle Bronze Age. During its rule by the Roman and Byzantine empires from the 2nd to the 7th centuries, the city formed part of the Provincia Arabia set up by the Roman Emperor Trajan to replace the Nabataean kingdom of Petra.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The main sites of Madaba:&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Church of Saint George which houses the famous Map of Madaba that was discovered in 1896 a mosaic of the 6th century representing a map of the Holy Land, sometimes called the &quot;Church of the Map&quot;. With two million pieces of colored stone, the map depicts hills, valleys and villages. (Entrance 1 JOD, not included in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Church of the Apostles, the ruins of this Byzantine church date to 578 CE, and are currently being restored. It includes a mosaic known as the &quot;Personification of the Sea&quot;, depicting a woman emerging from the sea, surrounded by mythical aquatic creatures and a hodgepodge of rams, bulls, parrots and exotic vegetation. The mosaic was signed by a mosaicist named Salamanios. (included in &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Church of San Giovanni Battista (Church of the takeoff of Giovanni Battista) that offers a magnificent view of the city as it is possible to climb up to the top of the bell tower (ticket, not included in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The city is rather nice and in addition to the visits of churches, it is quite pleasant to stroll around the city and nibble something in one the several traditional restaurants in the town.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Madaba/madaba mosque.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d54304.0835391128!2d35.7633807408465!3d31.71575236400819!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151cacd00bad3bc5:0x4d6d5834c1003e2b!2sMadaba!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564829017080!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 398, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'madaba'),
(1404, 'Desert Castles', 'Desert Castles', 'Desert Castles', 'Desert Castles', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Stretching East of Amman, the parched desert plain rolls on to Iraq and Saudi Arabia. This is a place where endless sand and barren basalt landscapes give proof to man’s ability to thrive under harsh conditions.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The discovery of flint hand-axes in this desert indicates that Paleolithic settlers inhabited the region around half a million years ago. But the most remarkable remains of human habitation are the palaces built by the Damascus-based Umayyad caliphs during the early days of Islam (VII-VIII centuries CE).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;During the height of the Umayyad dynasty, architecture flourished with the cultural exchange that accompanied growing trade routes. By 750 CE, when the Umayyad dynasty was overthrown by the Abbasids of Baghdad, a richly characteristic Muslim architecture was evolving, owing considerably to the cosmopolitan influence of builders and craftsmen drawn from Egypt, Mesopotamia and elsewhere throughout the region.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Today it is possible to see many relics of the early and medieval Islamic periods in Jordan. Dotted throughout the steppe-like terrain of eastern Jordan and the central hills are numerous historic ruins, including castles, forts, towers, baths, caravan inns and fortified palaces. Known collectively as the desert castles or desert palaces, they were originally part of a chain stretching from north of Damascus down to Khirbet al-Mafjar, near Ariha (or Jericho).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;en/qasr-al-kharanah/&quot;&gt;Qasr Al-Kharanah&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;en/qasr-amra/&quot;&gt;Qasr Amra&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Desert Castles/qasr-amra.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3202.960326365759!2d36.46056488753891!3d31.7285686252473!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b249e0321d58d:0xae2394f52625c2b!2sQasr al-Kharaneh!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1569247005481!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 395, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'desert-castles'),
(1405, 'Jordan River and Bethany', 'Jordan River and Bethany', 'Jordan River and Bethany', 'Jordan River and Bethany', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The Jordan River is a 251-kilometre-long (156 mi) river in the Middle East that flows roughly north to south through the Sea of Galilee and on to the Dead Sea. Jordan and the Golan Heights border the river to the east, while the West Bank and Israel lie to its west. Both Jordan and the West Bank take their names from the river.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The river holds major significance in Judaism and Christianity since the Bible says that the Israelites crossed it into the Promised Land and that Jesus of Nazareth was baptized by John the Baptist in it.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Bethany beyond the Jordan River, where John the Baptist preached and baptized during the early days of his ministry, has recently been revealed following archaeological surveys and excavations along the length of Wadi Al-Kharrar since 1996.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Combined evidence from the biblical text, Byzantine and medieval writers&#039; accounts, and most recent archaeological works, place the tradition of John the Baptist&#039;s mission, including the baptism of Jesus, adjacent to and directly east of the Jordan River.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan River/Jordan River website 800x500.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d1723499.3313860807!2d35.56573869965196!3d32.46708428012451!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151cf2b17acb4f8d:0xd2cc3c98dd2eaaf7!2sJordan River!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1567437278772!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 449, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'jordan-river-and-bethany'),
(1406, 'Amman', 'Amman', 'Amman', 'Amman', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Amman is the capital and most populous city of Jordan, and the country&#039;s economic, political and cultural centre. Situated in north-central Jordan, Amman is the administrative centre of the Amman Governorate. The city has a population of 4,007,526 and a land area of 1,680 square kilometers (648.7 square miles).  Today, Amman is considered to be among the most modernized Arab cities. It is a major tourist destination in the region, particularly among Arab and European tourists.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;<br> Amman is divided into two parts: the western part, not only geographically, full of nightclubs, pubs, central commerce, and the eastern part, which still preserves important archaeological sites, like the Citadel, the Roman Amphitheatre...as well as the typical Arab &quot;suq&quot; (traditional market).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The largest museum in Jordan is The Jordan Museum. It contains much of the valuable archaeological findings in the country, including some of the Dead Sea Scrolls, the Neolithic limestone statues of &#039;Ain Ghazal, and a copy of the Mesha Stele. Other museums include the Jordan National Gallery of Fine Arts, Jordan Archaeological Museum, The Children&#039;s Museum Jordan, The Martyrs&#039; Memorial and Museum, the Royal Automobile Museum, the Prophet Mohammad Museum, the Museum of Parliamentary Life, the Jordan Folklore Museum, and museums at the University of Jordan.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Amman is considered one of the most liberal and westernized cities in the Arab world. The city has become one of the most popular destinations for Western expatriates and college students who seek to live, study, or work in the Middle East.  The city&#039;s culinary scene has changed from its shawerma stands and falafel joints to embrace many popular western restaurants and fast-food outlets such as Asian fusion restaurants, French bistros and Italian trattorias.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;h5&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Amman/Royal Hotel.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d433870.8268373916!2d35.66743569022686!3d31.8354533233864!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x151b5fb85d7981af:0x631c30c0f8dc65e8!2sAmman!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1564595824430!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 388, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'amman'),
(1407, 'PV Travels Team', 'PV Travels Team', 'PV Travels Team', 'PV Travels Team', '&lt;div class=&quot;row &quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/khaled.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Khaled Nawafleh &quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;Black-text &quot;&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Khaled Nawafleh &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;PV Travels General Manager. Offering specialist, professional and competitive travel products&lt;/span&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/f1.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Fatima Ammar &quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;Black-text &quot;&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Fatima Ammar&lt;/strong&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Sales Department for Arabic, English, Italian and Spanish in PV Travels in Amman&lt;/span&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Screenshot_20191030-110610.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Fatima Assaf &quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;Black-text &quot;&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Fatima Assaf &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Sales Department for Arabic, French and English in PV Travels in Wadi Musa&lt;/span&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Screenshot_20191030-124413.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Ramzi Shamaseen &quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;Black-text &quot;&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Ramzi Shamaseen &lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Operations Department in Arabic and English in PV Travels in Wadi Musa&lt;/span&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Screenshot_20191030-124559.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Abeer Al-Hamadeen&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;Black-text &quot;&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Abeer Al-Hamadeen &lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Reservation Department for Arabic and English in PV Travels in Wadi Musa&lt;/span&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/PvtLogo2.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Farah Zitouni &quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;Black-text &quot;&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Farah Zitouni&lt;/strong&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Sales Department for Arabic, French and English in PV Travels in Wadi Musa&lt;/span&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Screenshot_20191030-122638.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Ahmad Al-Zoubi&quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;Black-text &quot;&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Ahmad Al-Zoubi &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Professional driver with more than 10 year of experience  in PV Travels in Wadi Musa&lt;/span&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-4 bd-3  d-pad&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;white shadow-box&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Anas.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Anas Al-Zoubi &quot; class=&quot;full-width&quot; width=&quot;281&quot; height=&quot;186&quot; /&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;Black-text &quot;&gt;  &lt;strong&gt;Anas Al-Zoubi &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-justify h-pad d-pad-l d-pad-r&quot; data-truncate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Professional driver with more than 3 year of experience  in PV Travels in Wadi Musa&lt;/span&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;align-center pad&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1363, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'pv-travels-team'),
(1408, 'Transportation in Jordan', 'Transportation in Jordan', 'Transportation in Jordan', 'Transportation in Jordan', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Car Rental&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Jordan has an excellent and expanding road network, and renting a car can be a good way to see the country. A driving license valid in your country of origin is acceptable, provided you have held it for at least one year. Driving is on the right. Road signs on the highways are in Arabic and English. Brown signs are designed for tourists. There are plenty of petrol stations in Amman and other cities, and on most highways. In PV travels we can arrange a rent-a-car before you travel to Jordan.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Buses&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Several companies offer charter bus and regular tours in a fleet of modern, air-conditioned coaches. If you&#039;re looking for easy transportation from Amman to some of Jordan&#039;s must-see tourism attractions you might consider taking the bus. JETT, one of Jordan&#039;s leading transportation companies, offers several trips (some daily and some weekly) to various destinations including Petra, the Dead Sea and Ma&#039;in Hot Springs in addition to Amman city tours in their brand-new buses.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Taxis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Taxis are inexpensive and often the most convenient form of transportation in Jordan, even over substantial distances, such as the trip between Amman and Aqaba. The white-painted &quot;service taxis&quot; ride fixed routes and are shared. Private taxis are painted yellow; they can be taken from ranks outside larger hotels, or hailed in the street. Taxis have meters, but these are not always used at night, so it is advisable to agree on the cost beforehand. The same applies to long journeys. Taxi drivers are friendly, know the city well, and usually speak English.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/testimonials/transportation3.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.663606793!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.265081424894323!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1572514329525!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1408, 'en', '', 'one col', 'transportation-in-jordan'),
(1409, 'المواصلات في الأردن', 'المواصلات في الأردن', 'Transportation in Jordan', 'Transportation in Jordan', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;md-7 align-justify d-pad-r&quot;&gt;&lt;h1&gt;المواصلات في الأردن&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2&gt;تأجير السيارات&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;يتمتع الأردن بشبكة طرق ممتازة ومتوسعة، وتأجير سيارة هو وسيلة رائعة لاستكشاف البلاد بوتيرتك الخاصة. تتوفر شركات تأجير السيارات الدولية والمحلية في المطار وفي جميع أنحاء عمان والمدن الرئيسية.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;سيارات الأجرة&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;سيارات الأجرة الصفراء متوفرة بكثرة في عمان والمدن الرئيسية. تأكد من أن السائق يستخدم العداد أو اتفق على السعر مسبقاً.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;الحافلات&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;تعمل شركة JETT كخدمة حافلات عامة تربط بين المدن الرئيسية في الأردن بما في ذلك عمان والعقبة والبتراء. كما تتوفر حافلات صغيرة محلية.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan/Jordan Info2.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1408, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'transportation-in-jordan');
INSERT INTO `en33_pages` (`id`, `name`, `title`, `meta_desc`, `meta_key`, `contents`, `published`, `lang_id`, `lang`, `icon`, `layout`, `url`) VALUES
(1410, 'Transporte en Jordania', 'Transporte en Jordania', 'Transporte en Jordania', 'Transporte en Jordania', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alquiler de Coches&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Jordania tiene una red de carreteras excelente y en expansión, y alquilar un automóvil puede ser una buena manera de ver el país. Una licencia de conducir válida en su país de origen es aceptable, siempre que la haya tenido durante al menos un año. Se conduce a la derecha. Las señales de tráfico en las carreteras están en árabe e inglés. Los carteles marrones están diseñados para turistas. Hay muchas estaciones de servicio en Amman y otras ciudades, y en la mayoría de las autopistas. En nuestra agencia de viajes PV Travels podemos organizar un alquiler de coche antes de viajar a Jordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Los Autobuses&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Varias compañías ofrecen autobuses chárter y recorridos regulares en una flota de busetas modernas con aire acondicionado. Si está buscando un transporte fácil desde Amman a algunas de las atracciones turísticas imprescindibles de Jordania, puede considerar tomar el autobús. JETT, una de las principales compañías de transporte de Jordania, ofrece varios viajes, incluidos Petra, el Mar Muerto y Ma&#039;in Hot Springs.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Los Taxis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Los taxis jordanos son baratos y económicos, incluso a distancias considerables, como el viaje entre Amman y Aqaba. Los &quot;taxis de servicio&quot; pintados de blanco recorren rutas fijas y son compartidos. Los taxis privados están pintados de amarillo; se pueden tomar de las filas fuera de los hoteles más grandes, o recibir llamadas en la calle. Tienen medidores, pero no siempre se usan por la noche, por lo que es aconsejable acordar el costo de antemano. Lo mismo se aplica a los viajes largos. Los taxistas son amigables, conocen bien la ciudad y generalmente hablan inglés.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/testimonials/transportation3.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.663606793!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.265081424894323!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1572514329525!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1408, 'es', '', 'one col', 'transporte-en-jordania'),
(1411, 'Transport en Jordanie', 'Transport en Jordanie', 'Transport en Jordanie', 'Transport en Jordanie', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location de Voiture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La Jordanie a un réseau routier excellent et en expansion, et louer une voiture peut être un bon moyen de visiter le pays. Un permis de conduire valide dans votre pays d&#039;origine est acceptable, à condition que vous l&#039;ayez depuis au moins un an. Cela conduit à droite. Les panneaux sur les routes sont en arabe et en anglais. Les panneaux marron sont conçus pour les touristes. Il existe de nombreuses stations-service à Amman et dans d&#039;autres villes, ainsi que sur la plupart des autoroutes. Dans notre agence de voyages PV Travels, nous pouvons organiser une location de voiture avant de voyager en Jordanie.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Les Bus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Plusieurs entreprises proposent des bus nolisés et des circuits réguliers dans une flotte de fourgonnettes modernes et climatisées. Si vous recherchez un moyen de transport facile entre Amman et certaines des attractions touristiques incontournables de la Jordanie, vous pouvez envisager de prendre le bus. JETT, l&#039;une des principales sociétés de transport jordaniennes, propose plusieurs voyages, notamment à Petra, à la Mer Morte et aux sources thermales de Ma&#039;in.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Les Taxis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Les taxis jordaniens sont bon marché et économiques, même sur des distances considérables, comme le trajet Amman-Aqaba. Les &quot;taxis de service&quot; peints en blanc suivent des itinéraires fixes et sont partagés. Les taxis privés sont peints en jaune; Ils peuvent être pris dans les rangs extérieurs aux grands hôtels ou recevoir des appels dans la rue. Ils ont des compteurs, mais ils ne sont pas toujours utilisés la nuit, il est donc conseillé de s’entendre à l’avance sur le coût. La même chose s&#039;applique aux longs voyages. Les chauffeurs de taxi sont sympathiques, connaissent bien la ville et parlent généralement anglais.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/testimonials/transportation3.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.663606793!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.265081424894323!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1572514329525!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1408, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'transport-en-jordanie'),
(1412, 'Trasporti in Giordania', 'Trasporti in Giordania', 'Trasporti in Giordania', 'Trasporti in Giordania', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;font-family: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-variant-ligatures: inherit; font-variant-caps: inherit; text-decoration-line: inherit;&quot;&gt;Noleggio Auto&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La Giordania ha una rete stradale eccellente e in espansione, e noleggiare un&#039;auto può essere un buon modo per vedere il paese. È accettabile una patente di guida valida nel proprio paese di origine, a condizione che sia stata posseduta per almeno un anno. Si guida a destra. I segnali stradali sulle strade sono in arabo e inglese. I segni marroni sono progettati per i turisti. Ci sono molte stazioni di servizio ad Amman e in altre città e sulla maggior parte delle autostrade. Nella nostra agenzia di viaggi PV Travels possiamo organizzare un noleggio auto prima di recarci in Giordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autobus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Diverse compagnie offrono autobus charter e tour regolari in una flotta di moderni furgoni con aria condizionata. Se stai cercando un trasporto facile da Amman ad alcune delle attrazioni turistiche imperdibili della Giordania, potresti prendere in considerazione l&#039;idea di prendere l&#039;autobus. JETT, una delle principali compagnie di trasporti della Giordania, offre diversi viaggi, tra cui Petra, il Mar Morto e Ma&#039;in Hot Springs.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Taxi&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;I taxi giordani sono economici ed economici, anche su distanze considerevoli, come il viaggio tra Amman e Aqaba. I &quot;taxi di servizio&quot; hanno dipinto percorsi fissi di viaggio bianchi e sono condivisi. I taxi privati ​​sono dipinti di giallo; Possono essere prelevati dai ranghi esterni agli hotel più grandi o ricevere chiamate per strada. Hanno contatori, ma non vengono sempre utilizzati di notte, quindi è consigliabile concordare preventivamente il costo. Lo stesso vale per i lunghi viaggi. I tassisti sono cordiali, conoscono bene la città e generalmente parlano inglese.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/testimonials/transportation3.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.663606793!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.265081424894323!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1572514329525!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1408, 'it', '', 'one col', 'trasporti-in-giordania'),
(1413, 'Jordan Pass', 'Jordan Pass', 'Jordan Pass', 'Jordan Pass', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt; is the ultimate sightseeing package that has been especially tailor-made for visitors to the beautiful Kingdom of Jordan. It gives pass holders the ability to make the most out of their trip visiting top sights and attractions while saving time, money and efforts.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Hassle-free prepaid entry to over 40 attractions in Jordan. Free downloadable digital brochures covering all of Jordan’s tourist attractions. Waiving of tourist entry visa fees if you purchase the Jordan Pass before arrival to Jordan and stay a minimum of three nights (4 days).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Simply show your ticket at the entrance of any attraction covered by the Pass where it’ll be scanned by our special readers. The Jordan Pass is valid for use within 12 months following date of purchase. But it will automatically expire after 2 weeks of the first time it is scanned in the first touristic attraction.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;The Jordan Pass comes in three categories to suit all kinds of visits. The package you choose depends on the number of days you wish to spend exploring Petra, a UNESCO World Heritage Site that encompasses a breathtaking landscape of pink-hued rock mountain carved into the rock more than 2,000 years ago.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1 day &lt;/strong&gt;visit to Petra&lt;strong&gt; 70 JOD&lt;/strong&gt; (approximately &lt;strong&gt;99 USD&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2 consecutive &lt;/strong&gt;visit days to Petra&lt;strong&gt; 75 JOD&lt;/strong&gt; (approximately &lt;strong&gt;106 USD&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 consecutive &lt;/strong&gt;visit days to Petra&lt;strong&gt; 80 JOD&lt;/strong&gt; (approximately &lt;strong&gt;113 USD&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/testimonials/jordanpass.png&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.663606793!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.265081424894323!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1572514329525!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1413, 'en', '', 'one col', 'jordan-pass'),
(1414, 'جوردان باس', 'جوردان باس', 'Jordan Pass', 'Jordan Pass', '<div class=\"row\"><div class=\"md-7 align-justify d-pad-r\"><h1>جوردان باس</h1><p>جوردان باس هو التذكرة الموحدة للسياح التي تتيح لهم زيارة أكثر من 40 موقعاً أثرياً في الأردن بما في ذلك البتراء.</p><p>يوفر جوردان باس المال والوقت والجهد، كما يعفي حامله من رسوم تأشيرة الدخول إذا تم شراؤه قبل الوصول والإقامة لمدة 3 ليالٍ على الأقل.</p></div><div class=\"md-5\"><img src=\"uploads/filemanager/Photos/Jordan/Jordan Info2.jpg\" class=\"full-width\" /></div></div>', 0, 1413, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'jordan-pass'),
(1415, 'Jordan Pass', 'Jordan Pass', 'Jordan Pass', 'Jordan Pass', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt; es lo último en paquetes turísticos especialmente diseñado para los visitantes del hermoso Reino de Jordania. Brinda a los titulares la capacidad de aprovechar al máximo su viaje visitando los principales lugares de interés y atracciones mientras ahorran tiempo, dinero y esfuerzos.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Entrada prepaga sin problemas a más de 40 atracciones en Jordania. Folletos digitales descargables gratuitos que cubren todas las atracciones turísticas de Jordania. Exención de las tarifas de visa de entrada turística si compra el Jordan Pass antes de llegar a Jordania y se queda un mínimo de tres noches (4 días).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Simplemente muestre su boleto en la entrada de cualquier atracción cubierta por el Jordan Pass, donde nuestros lectores especiales lo escanearán. El Jordan Pass es válido para su uso dentro de los 12 meses posteriores a la fecha de compra. Pero caducará automáticamente después de 2 semanas de la primera vez que se escanea en la primera atracción turística.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;El Jordan Pass viene en tres categorías para adaptarse a todo tipo de visitas. El paquete que elija depende de la cantidad de días que desee pasar explorando Petra, un sitio del Patrimonio Mundial de la UNESCO que abarca un impresionante paisaje de montaña rocosa de color rosa tallado en la roca hace más de 2.000 años.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;Visita de &lt;strong&gt;1 día&lt;/strong&gt; a Petra &lt;strong&gt;70 JOD&lt;/strong&gt; (aproximadamente &lt;strong&gt;99 USD&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2 días&lt;/strong&gt; de visita consecutiva a Petra &lt;strong&gt;75 JOD&lt;/strong&gt; (aproximadamente &lt;strong&gt;106 USD&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 días&lt;/strong&gt; de visita consecutiva a Petra &lt;strong&gt;80 JOD&lt;/strong&gt; (aproximadamente &lt;strong&gt;113 USD&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/testimonials/jordanpass.png&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.663606793!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.265081424894323!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1572514329525!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1413, 'es', '', 'one col', 'jordan-pass'),
(1416, 'Jordan Pass', 'Jordan Pass', 'Jordan Pass', 'Jordan Pass', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Le &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt; est le dernier en termes de forfaits spécialement conçus pour les visiteurs du magnifique royaume de Jordanie. Il donne aux propriétaires la possibilité de tirer le meilleur parti de leur voyage en visitant les principales attractions tout en économisant du temps, de l&#039;argent et des efforts.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Entrée prépayée sans problèmes dans plus de 40 attractions en Jordanie. Brochures numériques téléchargeables gratuitement couvrant toutes les attractions touristiques de la Jordanie. Exemption des frais de visa d’entrée touristique si vous achetez le Jordan Pass avant d’arriver en Jordanie et restez au moins trois nuits (4 jours).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Présentez simplement votre billet à l&#039;entrée de toute attraction couverte par le Jordan Pass, où nos lecteurs spéciaux le scanneront. Le Jordan Pass est valable pour une utilisation dans les 12 mois suivant la date d’achat. Mais il expirera automatiquement 2 semaines après sa première numérisation sur la première attraction touristique.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Le Jordan Pass se divise en trois catégories pour tous les types de visites. Le forfait que vous choisirez dépendra du nombre de jours que vous souhaitez consacrer à l&#039;exploration de Petra, site classé au patrimoine mondial de l&#039;UNESCO, qui comprend un impressionnant paysage de montagnes rocheuses roses sculptées dans le rocher il y a plus de 2 000 ans.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1 journée&lt;/strong&gt; de visite à Petra &lt;strong&gt;70 JOD&lt;/strong&gt; (environ &lt;strong&gt;99 USD&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2 jours &lt;/strong&gt;de visite consécutive à Petra &lt;strong&gt;75 JOD&lt;/strong&gt; (environ &lt;strong&gt;106 USD&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 jours&lt;/strong&gt; de visite consécutive à Petra &lt;strong&gt;80 JOD&lt;/strong&gt; (environ &lt;strong&gt;113 USD&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/testimonials/jordanpass.png&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.663606793!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.265081424894323!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1572514329525!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1413, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'jordan-pass'),
(1417, 'Jordan Pass', 'Jordan Pass', 'Jordan Pass', 'Jordan Pass', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Il &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jordanpass.jo/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Jordan Pass&lt;/a&gt; è l&#039;ultimo pacchetto turistico appositamente progettato per i visitatori del meraviglioso Regno di Giordania. Offre ai proprietari la possibilità di sfruttare al meglio il loro viaggio visitando le principali attrazioni e attrazioni risparmiando tempo, denaro e sforzi.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Ingresso prepagato senza problemi a più di 40 attrazioni in Giordania. Opuscoli digitali scaricabili gratuitamente che coprono tutte le attrazioni turistiche della Giordania. Esenzione delle tasse per il visto di ingresso turistico se si acquista il Jordan Pass prima di arrivare in Giordania e rimanere per un minimo di tre notti (4 giorni).&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Mostra semplicemente il tuo biglietto all&#039;ingresso di qualsiasi attrazione coperta dal Jordan Pass, dove i nostri lettori speciali lo scannerizzeranno. Jordan Pass è valido per l&#039;uso entro 12 mesi dalla data di acquisto. Ma scadrà automaticamente dopo 2 settimane dalla prima scansione alla prima attrazione turistica.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Il Jordan Pass è suddiviso in tre categorie per soddisfare tutti i tipi di visite. Il pacchetto che scegli dipende dal numero di giorni che vuoi trascorrere alla scoperta di Petra, un sito patrimonio mondiale dell&#039;UNESCO che comprende un impressionante paesaggio montuoso roccioso rosa scavato nella roccia oltre 2000 anni fa.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;ul&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1 giorno&lt;/strong&gt; di visita a Petra &lt;strong&gt;70 JOD&lt;/strong&gt; (circa &lt;strong&gt;99 USD&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2 giorni&lt;/strong&gt; di visita consecutiva a Petra &lt;strong&gt;75 JOD&lt;/strong&gt; (circa &lt;strong&gt;106 USD&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 giorni&lt;/strong&gt; di visita consecutiva a Petra &lt;strong&gt;80 JOD&lt;/strong&gt; (circa &lt;strong&gt;113 USD&lt;/strong&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\r\n&lt;/ul&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/testimonials/jordanpass.png&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.663606793!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.265081424894323!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1572514329525!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1413, 'it', '', 'one col', 'jordan-pass'),
(1418, 'Reasons To Visit Jordan', 'Reasons To Visit Jordan', 'Reasons To Visit Jordan', 'Reasons To Visit Jordan', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Jordan is a land steeped in history. It has been home to some of mankind&#039;s earliest settlements and villages; harboring hidden relics from the world&#039;s great civilizations.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Glorious ancient architecture, desert adventures, deep sea diving, local home stays, delicious Jordanian cooking, spectacular holy sites, the Red Sea and the Dead Sea are just some of the reasons to visit Jordan. As there are so many things to do in Jordan, we have picked a few favorites to offer a taste of what Jordan is all about.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Historic Treasures of Jordan&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Starting with what is widely considered to be Jordan’s most popular attraction, Petra is a historical and archaeological city located in the south of Jordan. Also known as ‘Rose City’ due to the coloring of the stone, the city’s main entrance is a breathtaking sight located at the end of a winding stone corridor.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Some of the most well-preserved archaeological sites of the Roman Empire stand in Jordan. Aside from the ruins of the Greco-Roman city of Gerasa in Jerash, be sure to visit the Citadel (for amazing city views) and the Roman Theatre, both located close to downtown Amman.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It’s Safe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;It is absolutely safe to travel in and around the country, independently or in a group. This Middle Eastern country looks to welcome 7 million a year by 2020. Here&#039;s why it&#039;s your turn to be enraptured by a country that offers sun, sea, sand dunes, the wonders of Petra and delicious lamb and yoghurt.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jordanian Hospitality &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;If Jordan is famous for only one thing, it is the hospitality and kindness of the Jordanian people. You’ll be happy to find that people are always prepared to help you and will go above and beyond in making sure that you are enjoying yourself as a guest in their country. Be prepared to receive many, many invitations for dinner and tea.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Food&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;There is more to Arabic cuisine than falafel and hummus. Traditional, home-cooked Jordanian food is some of the tastiest, and healthiest, that you will encounter in the region. Must-try dishes include rice- and meat-based Mansaf and Maqloube, and if you’re lucky enough to be travelling in the summer, then the assortment of colorful fresh salads, such as tabbouleh, will complement the meal well.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;From North to South, Jordan is Incredibly Diverse&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;When travelling around Jordan, the diversity of landscapes and people may surprise you. Experience the serene and humble lifestyle of the Bedouins in the desert of Wadi Rum by camping with them for a night, but don’t forget to explore what the progressive and fast city life in Amman has to offer as well.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/testimonials/food.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.663606793!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.265081424894323!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1572514329525!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1418, 'en', '', 'one col', 'reasons-to-visit-jordan'),
(1419, 'أسباب لزيارة الأردن', 'أسباب لزيارة الأردن', 'Reasons To Visit Jordan', 'Reasons To Visit Jordan', '<div class=\"row\"><div class=\"md-7 align-justify d-pad-r\"><h1>أسباب لزيارة الأردن</h1><p>الأردن أرض متجذرة في التاريخ. لقد كانت موطناً لبعض من أقدم المستوطنات والقرى البشرية، وتضم آثاراً مخفية من أعظم حضارات العالم.</p><p>الهندسة المعمارية القديمة المجيدة، والمغامرات الصحراوية، والغوص في أعماق البحار، والمأكولات الأردنية اللذيذة، والمواقع المقدسة المذهلة، والبحر الأحمر والبحر الميت هي فقط بعض من الأسباب لزيارة الأردن.</p><h2>الكنوز التاريخية</h2><p>تعتبر البتراء الوجهة السياحية الأكثر شهرة في الأردن، وهي مدينة تاريخية وأثرية تقع في جنوب الأردن وتعرف باسم المدينة الوردية.</p><h2>كرم الضيافة الأردني</h2><p>إذا كان الأردن مشهوراً بشيء واحد، فهو كرم ضيافة ولطف الشعب الأردني.</p></div><div class=\"md-5\"><img src=\"uploads/filemanager/Photos/testimonials/food.jpg\" class=\"full-width\" /></div></div>', 1, 1418, 'Ar', '', 'one col', 'reasons-to-visit-jordan'),
(1420, 'Razones Para Visitar Jordania', 'Razones Para Visitar Jordania', 'Razones Para Visitar Jordania', 'Razones Para Visitar Jordania', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Jordania es una tierra llena de historia. Ha sido el hogar de algunos de los primeros asentamientos y aldeas de la humanidad; que alberga reliquias ocultas de las grandes civilizaciones del mundo.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La arquitectura antigua gloriosa, las aventuras en el desierto, el buceo en aguas profundas, las estancias en hogares locales, la deliciosa cocina jordana, los lugares sagrados espectaculares, el Mar Rojo y el Mar Muerto son solo algunas de las razones para visitar Jordania. Como hay tantas cosas que hacer en Jordania, hemos elegido algunos favoritos para ofrecer una idea de lo que se trata Jordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tesoros Históricos de Jordania&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Comenzando con lo que se considera la atracción más popular de Jordania, Petra es una ciudad histórica y arqueológica ubicada en el Sur de Jordania. También conocida como &quot;Ciudad Rosa&quot; debido a la coloración de la piedra, la entrada principal de la ciudad es una vista impresionante ubicada al final de un sinuoso corredor de piedra.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Algunos de los sitios arqueológicos mejor conservados del Imperio Romano se encuentran en Jordania. Además de las ruinas de la ciudad grecorromana de Gerasa en Jerash, asegúrese de visitar la Ciudadela (para disfrutar de las increíbles vistas de la ciudad) y el Teatro Romano, ambos ubicados cerca del centro de Ammán.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Es Seguro&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Es absolutamente seguro viajar dentro y alrededor del país, independientemente o en grupo. Este país del Medio Oriente espera recibir 7 millones al año para 2020. Esta es la razón por la que te encantará un país que ofrece sol, mar, dunas de arena, las maravillas de Petra y un delicioso cordero y yogur.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hospitalidad Jordana&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Si Jordania es famosa por una sola cosa, es la hospitalidad y amabilidad del pueblo jordano. Te alegrará descubrir que las personas siempre están preparadas para ayudarte y harán todo lo posible para asegurarte de que disfrutas como invitado en su país. Esté preparado para recibir muchas, muchas invitaciones para la cena y el té.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;La Comida&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Hay más en la cocina árabe que el Falafel y el Hummus. La comida tradicional jordana casera es una de las más sabrosas y saludables que encontrarás en la región. Los platos que debes probar incluyen Mansaf y Maqloube a base de arroz y carne, y si tienes la suerte de viajar en verano, la variedad de coloridas ensaladas frescas, como Tabbouleh, complementará bien la comida.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;De Norte a Sur, Jordania es Increíblemente Diversa&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Al viajar por Jordania, la diversidad de paisajes y personas puede sorprenderte. Experimente el estilo de vida sereno y humilde de los beduinos en el desierto de Wadi Rum al acampar con ellos por una noche, pero no se olvide de explorar lo que la vida progresiva y rápida de la ciudad de Ammán también tiene para ofrecer.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/testimonials/food.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.663606793!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.265081424894323!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1572514329525!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1418, 'es', '', 'one col', 'razones-para-visitar-jordania'),
(1421, 'Raisons Pour Visiter la Jordanie', 'Raisons Pour Visiter la Jordanie', 'Raisons Pour Visiter la Jordanie', 'Raisons Pour Visiter la Jordanie', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La Jordanie est une terre chargée d&#039;histoire. Il a abrité certaines des premières colonies et villages de l&#039;humanité; qui abrite des vestiges cachés des grandes civilisations du monde.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Une ancienne architecture glorieuse, des aventures dans le désert, la plongée en haute mer, des séjours chez l&#039;habitant, une cuisine jordanienne délicieuse, des lieux sacrés spectaculaires, la mer Rouge et la mer Morte sont quelques-unes des raisons pour lesquelles vous rendre en Jordanie. Comme il y a tant de choses à faire en Jordanie, nous avons choisi quelques favoris pour vous donner une idée de ce qu&#039;est la Jordanie.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Les Trésors Historiques de la Jordanie&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;En commençant par ce qui est considéré comme l&#039;attraction la plus populaire de Jordanie, Petra est une ville historique et archéologique située dans le sud de la Jordanie. Également connue sous le nom de &quot;Ville rose&quot; en raison de la couleur de la pierre, l&#039;entrée principale de la ville est une vue impressionnante située au bout d&#039;un couloir de pierre sinueux.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Certains des sites archéologiques les mieux conservés de l&#039;empire romain se trouvent en Jordanie. En plus des ruines de la ville gréco-romaine de Gerasa à Jerash, n&#039;oubliez pas de visiter la citadelle (pour profiter des vues incroyables sur la ville) et le théâtre romain, tous deux situés près du centre d&#039;Amman.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;C&#039;Est Sûr&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Il est absolument sans danger de voyager dans et autour du pays, seul ou en groupe. Ce pays du Moyen-Orient s&#039;attend à en recevoir 7 millions par an d&#039;ici à 2020. C&#039;est pourquoi vous allez adorer un pays qui offre soleil, mer, dunes de sable, merveilles de Pétra et un délicieux agneau et yaourt.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;L&#039;Hospitalité Jordanienne&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Si la Jordanie n’est célèbre que pour une chose, c’est l’hospitalité et la gentillesse du peuple jordanien. Vous serez heureux de découvrir que les gens sont toujours prêts à vous aider et feront tout leur possible pour que vous profitiez pleinement de votre séjour dans leur pays. Préparez-vous à recevoir de nombreuses invitations pour le dîner et le thé.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Le Gastronomie&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Falafel et Houmous ne se résument pas à la cuisine arabe. La cuisine jordanienne faite maison est l’un des plats les plus savoureux et les plus sains que vous trouverez dans la région. Mansaf et Maqloube sont des plats à base de riz et de viande. Si vous avez la chance de voyager en été, la variété de salades fraîches et colorées, telles que le Taboulé, viendra bien compléter le repas.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Du Nord au Sud, la Jordanie est Incroyablement Diversifiée&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Lorsque vous voyagez en Jordanie, la diversité des paysages et des habitants peut vous surprendre. Découvrez le style de vie serein et humble des Bédouins dans le désert du Wadi Rum lorsque vous campez avec eux pour une nuit, mais n&#039;oubliez pas d&#039;explorer ce que la vie progressive et rapide de la ville d&#039;Amman a également à offrir.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/testimonials/food.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.663606793!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.265081424894323!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1572514329525!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1418, 'fr', '', 'one col', 'raisons-pour-visiter-la-jordanie'),
(1422, 'Ragioni Per Visitare la Giordania', 'Ragioni Per Visitare la Giordania', 'Ragioni Per Visitare la Giordania', 'Ragioni Per Visitare la Giordania', '&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-7&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;La Giordania è una terra ricca di storia. Ha ospitato alcuni dei primi insediamenti e villaggi dell&#039;umanità; che ospita reliquie nascoste delle grandi civiltà del mondo.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Gloriosa architettura antica, avventure nel deserto, immersioni in acque profonde, soggiorni nelle case locali, deliziosa cucina giordana, spettacolari luoghi sacri, il Mar Rosso e il Mar Morto sono solo alcuni dei motivi per visitare la Giordania. Dato che ci sono così tante cose da fare in Giordania, abbiamo scelto alcuni dei preferiti per offrire un&#039;idea di cosa sia la Giordania.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;I Tesori Storici della Giordania&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;A partire da quella che è considerata l&#039;attrazione più popolare della Giordania, Petra è una città storica e archeologica situata nel sud della Giordania. Conosciuta anche come &quot;Città rosa&quot; a causa della colorazione della pietra, l&#039;ingresso principale della città è uno spettacolo impressionante situato alla fine di un tortuoso corridoio di pietra.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Alcuni dei siti archeologici meglio conservati dell&#039;Impero Romano si trovano in Giordania. Oltre alle rovine della città greco-romana di Gerasa a Jerash, assicurati di visitare la Cittadella (per godere delle incredibili viste della città) e il Teatro Romano, entrambi situati vicino al centro di Amman.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;È al Sicuro&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;È assolutamente sicuro viaggiare all&#039;interno e intorno al paese, indipendentemente o in gruppo. Questo paese del Medio Oriente prevede di ricevere 7 milioni all&#039;anno entro il 2020. Ecco perché amerai un paese che offre sole, mare, dune di sabbia, le meraviglie di Petra e un delizioso agnello e yogurt.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ospitalità Giordana&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Se la Giordania è famosa solo per una cosa, è l&#039;ospitalità e la gentilezza del popolo giordano. Sarai felice di scoprire che le persone sono sempre pronte ad aiutarti e faranno tutto il possibile per assicurarti di divertirti come ospite nel loro paese. Preparati a ricevere molti, molti inviti per la cena e il tè.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Il Cibo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;C&#039;è di più nella cucina araba di Falafel e Hummus. Il cibo tradizionale giordano fatto in casa è uno dei più gustosi e salutari che troverai nella regione. I piatti che dovresti provare includono Mansaf e Maqloube a base di riso e carne e, se sei abbastanza fortunato da viaggiare in estate, la varietà di insalate fresche colorate, come Tabbouleh, completerà bene il pasto.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Da nord a sud, la Giordania è Incredibilmente Diversificata&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;p&gt;Quando viaggi attraverso la Giordania, la diversità dei paesaggi e delle persone può sorprenderti. Sperimenta lo stile di vita sereno e umile dei beduini nel deserto del Wadi Rum durante il campeggio con loro per una notte, ma non dimenticare di esplorare ciò che la vita progressiva e veloce della città di Amman ha anche da offrire.&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-5 d-pad-t&quot;&gt; &lt;img class=&quot;full-width&quot; src=&quot;uploads/filemanager/Photos/testimonials/food.jpg&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;div class=&quot;md-12&quot;&gt; \r\n&lt;p&gt; &lt;iframe width=&quot;100%&quot; height=&quot;300&quot; style=&quot;border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3492247.663606793!2d34.87836949724749!3d31.265081424894323!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x15006f476664de99:0x8d285b0751264e99!2sJordan!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sjo!4v1572514329525!5m2!1sen!2sjo&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;allowfullscreen&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;\r\n&lt;/div&gt;', 1, 1418, 'it', '', 'one col', 'ragioni-per-visitare-la-giordania');
INSERT INTO `en33_pages` (`id`, `name`, `title`, `meta_desc`, `meta_key`, `contents`, `published`, `lang_id`, `lang`, `icon`, `layout`, `url`) VALUES
